var e={level:`B1`,type:`true-false`,questions:[{id:`b1-tf-001`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: 'because of her job', 'now she has many friends', 'calls them every weekend'.`,passage:`Sara moved to Canada two years ago because of her job. At first she felt lonely, but now she has many friends. She has never been so happy, although she still misses her family and calls them every weekend.`,statements:[{text:`Sara moved to Canada for work.`,answer:!0},{text:`She still feels lonely.`,answer:!1},{text:`She never calls her family.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-002`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: 'cheaper than driving' and 'some people think it is dangerous'.`,passage:`Cycling to work is becoming more popular in big cities. It is cheaper than driving and it is also good for your health. However, some people think it is dangerous because there are not enough bike lanes.`,statements:[{text:`Cycling is more expensive than driving.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people worry about safety.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-003`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'I've been really busy at work', 'I've had to go there three times already', 'my sister recommended' and 'Sunday is fine too'.`,passage:`Hi Megan, thanks for your email. I'm sorry I didn't reply sooner, but I've been really busy at work this month. My company has just opened a new office in Leeds, and I've had to go there three times already. The trains are often late, so I usually take my laptop and work during the journey. Next weekend I'm free at last. Would you like to meet for lunch on Saturday? There's a new Thai restaurant near the station which my sister recommended. If you can't come on Saturday, Sunday is fine too. Let me know! Love, Hannah`,statements:[{text:`Hannah has been busy at work recently.`,answer:!0},{text:`Hannah has visited the Leeds office only once.`,answer:!1},{text:`Hannah's brother recommended the restaurant.`,answer:!1},{text:`Hannah could also meet on Sunday.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-004`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'expected about two thousand visitors, but more than five thousand people came', 'stay in tents', 'two famous groups came from Madrid' and 'organise it again next year'.`,passage:`Last summer, a small town in the north of Spain held its first music festival. The organisers expected about two thousand visitors, but more than five thousand people came. Local hotels were full, so many visitors had to stay in tents in a field near the river. Most of the bands were from the region, although two famous groups came from Madrid. Unfortunately, it rained heavily on the second day and one concert was cancelled. In spite of the weather, the festival was a big success, and the town council has decided to organise it again next year.`,statements:[{text:`The organisers expected more than five thousand visitors.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some visitors slept in tents.`,answer:!0},{text:`All the bands came from the local area.`,answer:!1},{text:`There will be another festival next year.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-005`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'rode his bicycle', 'he loved it anyway', 'He retired fifteen years ago' and 'He still rides his old bicycle'.`,passage:`My grandfather, Ken, used to work as a postman in a small village. Every morning he got up at five o'clock and rode his bicycle along the country roads. He knew everyone in the village, and people often invited him in for a cup of tea. He says that the job was hard in winter, when the roads were covered in snow, but he loved it anyway. He retired fifteen years ago. Now he spends most of his time in his garden, where he grows tomatoes, beans and potatoes. He still rides his old bicycle to the shops every day.`,statements:[{text:`Ken delivered letters by bicycle.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ken didn't enjoy his job because of the winter.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ken stopped working fifteen years ago.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ken doesn't use his bicycle any more.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-006`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'aged six to nine', 'The tyres are new', 'A helmet is included for free' and 'we can't deliver it'.`,passage:`FOR SALE: Kids' bike, blue, suitable for children aged six to nine. It has been used for only one year and it is in very good condition. The tyres are new and the brakes were checked last month. We are selling it because our son has grown too tall for it. The price is £60, but we will also accept a reasonable offer. A helmet is included for free. Please call Tom after 6 p.m. on weekdays or any time at the weekend. You can come and look at the bike before you decide. Sorry, we can't deliver it.`,statements:[{text:`The bike is suitable for teenagers.`,answer:!1},{text:`The bike has new tyres.`,answer:!0},{text:`You have to pay extra for the helmet.`,answer:!1},{text:`The sellers will bring the bike to your house.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-007`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'every Saturday morning', 'helps the staff to feed the cats', 'Now she isn't afraid of them at all' and 'become a vet'.`,passage:`Lucy has always loved animals, so last year she started volunteering at an animal shelter near her home. She goes there every Saturday morning. Her main job is to walk the dogs and clean their cages, but sometimes she also helps the staff to feed the cats. At first she was a bit nervous because some of the dogs were big and noisy. Now she isn't afraid of them at all. Lucy says the best moment is when an animal finds a new family. She is hoping to study to become a vet when she finishes school.`,statements:[{text:`Lucy works at the shelter once a week.`,answer:!0},{text:`Lucy sometimes feeds the cats.`,answer:!0},{text:`Lucy is still afraid of the big dogs.`,answer:!1},{text:`Lucy wants to become a teacher.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-008`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'close for four weeks', 'stay open until 8 p.m. instead of 6 p.m.', 'will meet at the community centre' and 'you can still download e-books'.`,passage:`The Riverside Library is going to close for four weeks from 1st March because the building needs a new roof. During this time, readers can borrow books from the City Library on King Street, which will stay open until 8 p.m. instead of 6 p.m. Books which you borrowed from Riverside can be returned to any library in the city. The children's reading club will meet at the community centre instead of the library. The library's website and online services will work as usual, so you can still download e-books and magazines. We are sorry for any problems this may cause.`,statements:[{text:`The Riverside Library will close for four months.`,answer:!1},{text:`The City Library will open longer hours.`,answer:!0},{text:`The children's reading club has been cancelled.`,answer:!1},{text:`E-books will still be available online.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-009`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'had never cooked a real meal', 'soon he started to feel tired', 'was a disaster' and 'the most popular dish in the flat'.`,passage:`Daniel had never cooked a real meal before he left home to go to university. In his first month, he ate pizza and instant noodles almost every day and soon he started to feel tired. So he decided to learn to cook. He watched online videos and asked his mother for some easy recipes. His first attempt, a chicken curry, was a disaster because he put in too much salt. But he didn't give up. Now, two years later, he cooks for his flatmates twice a week, and his vegetable soup is the most popular dish in the flat.`,statements:[{text:`Daniel couldn't cook when he started university.`,answer:!0},{text:`Daniel felt healthier after eating pizza and noodles.`,answer:!1},{text:`His first curry was very good.`,answer:!1},{text:`His flatmates like his soup.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-010`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'a growing number of tourists prefer walking tours', 'a small group', 'people usually give the guide some money' and 'last about two hours'.`,passage:`Many people think that the best way to see a new city is to take a bus tour. However, a growing number of tourists prefer walking tours. On a walking tour, a local guide takes a small group through the streets and tells them stories about the history of the area. You can stop to take photos, visit small shops and try local food. Some walking tours are free, but at the end people usually give the guide some money if they enjoyed it. Walking tours normally last about two hours, so it's a good idea to wear comfortable shoes.`,statements:[{text:`Walking tours are becoming less popular.`,answer:!1},{text:`Walking tours are usually for small groups.`,answer:!0},{text:`People often pay the guide at the end of a free tour.`,answer:!0},{text:`Walking tours usually last all day.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-011`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'bought from your online shop', 'the box was damaged', 'nobody answered' and 'I have attached a photo'.`,passage:`Dear Mr Patel, I am writing to complain about a coffee machine which I bought from your online shop on 10th May. When it arrived, the box was damaged and the glass jug was broken. I called your customer service number twice, but nobody answered. I also sent an email last week, but I haven't received a reply yet. I would like you to send me a new jug as soon as possible, or give me my money back. I have attached a photo of the broken jug to this email. I look forward to hearing from you. Yours sincerely, Rachel Green`,statements:[{text:`Rachel bought the coffee machine online.`,answer:!0},{text:`The box arrived in perfect condition.`,answer:!1},{text:`A customer service assistant answered Rachel's call.`,answer:!1},{text:`Rachel has sent a photo with her email.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-012`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Five years ago', 'it doesn't cost anything', 'others walk most of the way' and 'I've already made lots of new friends'.`,passage:`Running has become very popular in my town. Five years ago, a group of friends started meeting in the park every Sunday morning to run together. Now more than a hundred people join them every week. The group is open to everyone, and it doesn't cost anything. Some members run five kilometres in less than twenty minutes, while others walk most of the way. Nobody minds how fast you are. After the run, many people go to the café next to the park for breakfast. I joined the group last spring, and I've already made lots of new friends.`,statements:[{text:`The group started last year.`,answer:!1},{text:`You have to pay to join the group.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people walk instead of running.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer has met new people through the group.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-013`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'sometimes she has to work at night', 'it is difficult to sleep during the day', 'worked in a bank for three years' and 'Next year she is going to start a course'.`,passage:`Amira works as a nurse in a busy hospital in Manchester. She usually works long shifts of twelve hours, and sometimes she has to work at night. She says the night shifts are the hardest because it is difficult to sleep during the day. However, she loves her job because she can help people every day. Before she became a nurse, Amira worked in a bank for three years, but she found the work boring. She went back to university when she was twenty-five. Next year she is going to start a course to become a children's nurse.`,statements:[{text:`Amira sometimes works at night.`,answer:!0},{text:`Amira finds it easy to sleep during the day.`,answer:!1},{text:`Amira used to work in a bank.`,answer:!0},{text:`Amira has already finished a course to become a children's nurse.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-014`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'opened two months ago', 'you should book a table, especially at the weekend', 'The desserts were a little disappointing' and 'it isn't the best place for a quiet conversation'.`,passage:`The Green Leaf is a new vegetarian restaurant in the city centre. It opened two months ago and it is already very popular, so you should book a table, especially at the weekend. The menu is small but everything is fresh, and the vegetables come from a farm just outside the city. I had the mushroom pie, which was delicious, and my friend loved her pasta with spinach. The desserts were a little disappointing, though. The prices are reasonable and the staff are friendly. My only complaint is that it was very noisy, so it isn't the best place for a quiet conversation.`,statements:[{text:`The restaurant has been open for two years.`,answer:!1},{text:`It is a good idea to book at the weekend.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer thought the desserts were excellent.`,answer:!1},{text:`The restaurant is a good place for a quiet chat.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-015`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'his uncle gave him an old guitar for his birthday', 'At first he didn't play it much', 'two birthday parties and a school concert' and 'it is much harder'.`,passage:`When Oliver was twelve, his uncle gave him an old guitar for his birthday. At first he didn't play it much, but one day he heard a song on the radio and decided to learn it. He practised every evening after school, and after a few weeks he could play the whole song. Since then, he has learned more than fifty songs. Last year he started a band with three friends from school. They have played at two birthday parties and a school concert. Oliver wants to write his own songs, but he says it is much harder than playing other people's music.`,statements:[{text:`Oliver's guitar was a present.`,answer:!0},{text:`Oliver started playing every day as soon as he got the guitar.`,answer:!1},{text:`Oliver's band has played at a wedding.`,answer:!1},{text:`Oliver finds writing songs difficult.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-016`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'more productive at home because it is quieter', 'feel lonely because they don't see their colleagues', 'others find it hard to stop working' and 'taking regular breaks'.`,passage:`More and more people are working from home at least one day a week. Many workers say they like it because they don't have to travel to the office and they can spend more time with their families. Some also say they are more productive at home because it is quieter. However, working from home is not perfect. Some people feel lonely because they don't see their colleagues, and others find it hard to stop working in the evening. Experts suggest having a special place in your home for work and taking regular breaks during the day.`,statements:[{text:`Some people work better at home because it is quieter.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some home workers miss their colleagues.`,answer:!0},{text:`Everyone finds it easy to stop working in the evening.`,answer:!1},{text:`Experts say you should work without breaks.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-017`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'the coach will leave at 8.15', 'next to a lake', 'the campsite will provide them' and 'there is no electricity at the campsite'.`,passage:`Hi everyone! Just a quick message about the camping trip next weekend. We're meeting outside the school at 8 a.m. on Saturday, and the coach will leave at 8.15, so please don't be late. The campsite is about two hours away, next to a lake. Remember to bring a sleeping bag, warm clothes and a waterproof jacket, because the weather forecast says it might rain. You don't need to bring tents, as the campsite will provide them. Mobile phones are allowed, but there is no electricity at the campsite, so bring a power bank if you have one. See you on Saturday! Mr Evans`,statements:[{text:`The coach will leave at 8 a.m.`,answer:!1},{text:`The campsite is near a lake.`,answer:!0},{text:`Students need to bring their own tents.`,answer:!1},{text:`There is no electricity at the campsite.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-018`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Her father was a fisherman', 'to study art', 'she soon got used to the city' and 'next month she is opening her own gallery'.`,passage:`Maria grew up in a small fishing village in Portugal. Her father was a fisherman, and as a child she often went out on his boat early in the morning. When she was eighteen, she moved to Lisbon to study art. At first she missed the sea and the quiet life of the village, but she soon got used to the city. Today Maria is a successful painter. Most of her paintings show boats, beaches and fishermen from her home village. She has had exhibitions in Lisbon, Paris and London, and next month she is opening her own gallery.`,statements:[{text:`Maria's father worked as a fisherman.`,answer:!0},{text:`Maria went to Lisbon to study music.`,answer:!1},{text:`Maria never got used to life in the city.`,answer:!1},{text:`Maria already has her own gallery.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-019`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Tuesday and Thursday evenings', 'You don't need a partner', '£5' each or '£35 for ten classes', and 'Your first class is free'.`,passage:`Do you want to get fit but hate going to the gym? Then try our new dance classes at Sunnyside Sports Centre! Classes are on Tuesday and Thursday evenings from 7 to 8 p.m. You don't need a partner and you don't need any experience, because our teachers will show you all the steps. Each class costs £5, or you can pay £35 for ten classes. Just wear comfortable clothes and bring a bottle of water. Your first class is free, so why not come and try it? For more information, visit our website or ask at reception.`,statements:[{text:`The classes are on Mondays and Wednesdays.`,answer:!1},{text:`You must bring a partner to the class.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ten classes cost less than ten single classes.`,answer:!0},{text:`You don't pay for your first class.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-020`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'I woke up an hour late', 'I missed the bus', 'I had left my umbrella at home' and 'the meeting had been moved to the afternoon'.`,passage:`Yesterday was a terrible day for me. My alarm didn't ring, so I woke up an hour late. I got dressed quickly and ran to the bus stop, but I missed the bus by one minute. While I was waiting for the next one, it started to rain and I realised I had left my umbrella at home. When I finally arrived at the office, I was completely wet. Then my boss told me that the important meeting had been moved to the afternoon. So I didn't need to hurry after all! In the evening I went to bed early.`,statements:[{text:`The writer woke up late.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer caught the bus.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer didn't have an umbrella.`,answer:!0},{text:`The meeting happened in the morning.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-021`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'helps plants to produce fruit and seeds', 'the number of bees has fallen', 'Scientists think this is because of chemicals' and 'you can grow flowers'.`,passage:`Bees are very important for our planet. They carry pollen from one flower to another, which helps plants to produce fruit and seeds. Without bees, we wouldn't have many of the fruits and vegetables that we eat every day. Unfortunately, the number of bees has fallen in many countries in recent years. Scientists think this is because of chemicals used on farms and the loss of wild flowers. There are some simple things that everyone can do to help. For example, you can grow flowers in your garden or on your balcony, and you should avoid using chemicals on your plants.`,statements:[{text:`Bees help plants to produce fruit.`,answer:!0},{text:`The number of bees has gone up recently.`,answer:!1},{text:`Scientists don't know anything about the reasons for the problem.`,answer:!1},{text:`People can help bees by growing flowers.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-022`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'their first trip to Asia', 'took the fast train to Kyoto', 'Jake's favourite part of the trip was the food' and 'They are already planning to go back'.`,passage:`Jake and his wife Emma have just come back from a two-week holiday in Japan. It was their first trip to Asia. They spent the first week in Tokyo, where they visited museums, temples and the famous fish market. Then they took the fast train to Kyoto, which only took about two hours. Jake's favourite part of the trip was the food, especially the sushi. Emma enjoyed staying in a traditional hotel with paper walls. The only problem was the language, because they didn't speak any Japanese, but people were very helpful. They are already planning to go back.`,statements:[{text:`Jake and Emma had been to Asia many times before.`,answer:!1},{text:`They travelled from Tokyo to Kyoto by train.`,answer:!0},{text:`Emma's favourite thing was the sushi.`,answer:!1},{text:`They don't want to visit Japan again.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-023`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'from next term', 'They will be allowed to use them at lunchtime', 'phones stop students from concentrating' and 'others are worried'.`,passage:`Our school is going to have a new rule about mobile phones from next term. Students will have to switch off their phones and keep them in their bags during lessons. They will be allowed to use them at lunchtime, but not in the classrooms. Teachers say that phones stop students from concentrating, and that some students have been using them to cheat in tests. Some parents agree with the rule, but others are worried because they want to be able to contact their children. If a student needs to call home, they can use the phone in the school office.`,statements:[{text:`The new rule will start next term.`,answer:!0},{text:`Students won't be able to use their phones at lunchtime.`,answer:!1},{text:`Teachers think phones make it hard for students to concentrate.`,answer:!0},{text:`All parents are happy with the new rule.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-024`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'She trained for three months', 'it was cold and foggy at the top', 'four hours to reach the top and three hours to come down' and 'she felt very proud'.`,passage:`Sophie had always wanted to climb a mountain, so last August she decided to climb Ben Nevis, the highest mountain in Britain. She trained for three months before the climb by walking in the hills near her home every weekend. On the day, she started walking at seven in the morning. The weather was sunny at the bottom, but it was cold and foggy at the top, so she couldn't see much. It took her four hours to reach the top and three hours to come down. Her legs hurt for days afterwards, but she felt very proud.`,statements:[{text:`Sophie climbed the mountain without any training.`,answer:!1},{text:`The weather was sunny at the top.`,answer:!1},{text:`Coming down took less time than going up.`,answer:!0},{text:`Sophie was pleased with what she had done.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-025`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'the first computer games', 'Visitors can play with some of the toys', 'open until the end of September' and 'children under five can enter for free'.`,passage:`The city museum has opened a new exhibition about the history of toys. It shows more than three hundred toys from the last two centuries, including wooden trains, old dolls and the first computer games. Visitors can play with some of the toys in a special room, which is very popular with children. The exhibition will be open until the end of September. Tickets cost £8 for adults and £4 for children, but children under five can enter for free. On Sunday afternoons, there are special activities for families, such as making simple toys from paper.`,statements:[{text:`The exhibition includes early computer games.`,answer:!0},{text:`Visitors are not allowed to touch any of the toys.`,answer:!1},{text:`The exhibition will stay open all year.`,answer:!1},{text:`A three-year-old child doesn't need a ticket.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-026`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'next Saturday', 'I still have to take the bed apart', 'he has hurt his back' and 'let me know by Thursday'.`,passage:`Hi Josh, I'm writing to ask for your help. I'm moving to a new flat next Saturday and I need someone with a car to help me carry some boxes. I've already packed most of my things, but I still have to take the bed apart. My brother was going to help, but he has hurt his back playing football, so he can't lift anything heavy. The new flat is only ten minutes from my old one, so it shouldn't take more than three hours. I'll buy pizza for lunch to say thank you! Can you let me know by Thursday? Thanks, Ben`,statements:[{text:`Ben is moving next Sunday.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ben hasn't taken his bed apart yet.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ben's brother has hurt his leg.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ben would like an answer before Friday.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-027`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'it arrived in Europe in the seventeenth century', 'only rich people could buy it', 'green tea with fresh mint and sugar' and 'drinking tea may be good for your health'.`,passage:`Tea is one of the most popular drinks in the world. People in China have been drinking it for thousands of years, and it arrived in Europe in the seventeenth century. At first it was very expensive, so only rich people could buy it. Today, tea is cheap and people drink it in many different ways. In Britain, most people add milk to their tea, while in Morocco people often drink green tea with fresh mint and sugar. In some parts of India, tea is cooked with milk and spices. Some studies suggest that drinking tea may be good for your health.`,statements:[{text:`Tea arrived in Europe thousands of years ago.`,answer:!1},{text:`In the past, tea was too expensive for most people.`,answer:!0},{text:`In Morocco, people usually drink tea with milk.`,answer:!1},{text:`Tea may have some health benefits.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-028`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'for ten years', 'very hot, especially in summer', 'his wife does all the cooking at home' and 'he wanted to be a pilot'.`,passage:`Paul has worked as a chef in the same Italian restaurant for ten years. He starts work at eleven in the morning and often doesn't finish until midnight. The kitchen is small and very hot, especially in summer, but Paul enjoys the busy atmosphere. His favourite dish to cook is fresh pasta with seafood. On his days off, he doesn't cook at all; his wife does all the cooking at home. Paul says that when he was a boy, he wanted to be a pilot. He started cooking only because he needed a part-time job when he was a student.`,statements:[{text:`Paul has had the same job for ten years.`,answer:!0},{text:`The kitchen gets very hot in summer.`,answer:!0},{text:`Paul's wife cooks at home on his days off.`,answer:!0},{text:`Paul wanted to be a chef when he was a child.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-029`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Every year in May', 'wins the cheese', 'more than two hundred years' and 'an ambulance always waits at the bottom of the hill'.`,passage:`The village of Ashford is famous for its annual cheese-rolling race. Every year in May, people run down a steep hill after a large round cheese. The first person to reach the bottom wins the cheese. The race has taken place for more than two hundred years, and it attracts visitors from all over the world. Many runners fall over because the hill is so steep, and some of them get hurt. For this reason, an ambulance always waits at the bottom of the hill. Children can't take part in the main race, but there is a special uphill race for them.`,statements:[{text:`The race takes place every month.`,answer:!1},{text:`The winner gets a prize of money.`,answer:!1},{text:`The race started about twenty years ago.`,answer:!1},{text:`An ambulance is always ready during the race.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-030`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'next door to you', 'for two weeks', 'every two or three days' and 'You don't need to go inside the house'.`,passage:`Hello Mrs Taylor, my name is Lily and I live at number 12, next door to you. I'm writing because I'm going on holiday to Greece for two weeks from Monday, and I wonder if you could help me. Could you water the plants in my garden while I'm away? They need water every two or three days, especially if it's hot. I'll leave a key under the flowerpot by the back door. You don't need to go inside the house. I'll bring you back some Greek honey to say thank you. Please call me if there's a problem. Best wishes, Lily`,statements:[{text:`Lily lives next to Mrs Taylor.`,answer:!0},{text:`Lily is going away for one week.`,answer:!1},{text:`The plants need water every few days.`,answer:!0},{text:`Mrs Taylor doesn't need to enter the house.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-031`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'most of them only get six or seven', 'The light from the screen makes it harder', 'can also make people feel stressed' and 'going to sleep at the same time every night'.`,passage:`Sleep is very important for teenagers. Doctors say that people between thirteen and eighteen need about nine hours of sleep every night, but most of them only get six or seven. One reason is that many teenagers use their phones or computers in bed. The light from the screen makes it harder for the brain to fall asleep. Lack of sleep can make it difficult to concentrate at school and can also make people feel stressed. Experts recommend switching off all screens at least an hour before going to bed and going to sleep at the same time every night.`,statements:[{text:`Most teenagers get nine hours of sleep a night.`,answer:!1},{text:`The light from screens can make it harder to sleep.`,answer:!0},{text:`Not sleeping enough can cause stress.`,answer:!0},{text:`Experts say teenagers should go to bed at the same time every night.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-032`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'for the first time', 'six months before', 'a huge stadium' and 'I didn't get home until two in the morning'.`,passage:`Last month I went to see my favourite band in concert for the first time. I bought the tickets six months before, as soon as they went on sale, because I knew they would sell out quickly. The concert was in a huge stadium and there were about forty thousand people there. We arrived three hours early to get a good place near the stage. The band played for two and a half hours and they played all my favourite songs. The only bad thing was that the trains home were so crowded that I didn't get home until two in the morning.`,statements:[{text:`The writer had never seen the band live before.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer bought the tickets early.`,answer:!0},{text:`The concert took place in a small club.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer got home soon after the concert.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-033`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'He lives with an Irish family', 'in the afternoons he works part-time in a café', 'the most difficult thing is understanding people when they speak quickly' and 'it rains much more than in his home town'.`,passage:`Hiroshi is a student from Japan who is spending a year in Dublin to improve his English. He lives with an Irish family, the Murphys, who have two young children. In the mornings, he goes to a language school in the city centre, and in the afternoons he works part-time in a café. He says that the most difficult thing is understanding people when they speak quickly. He has also had to get used to the weather, because it rains much more than in his home town. However, he really enjoys living with the Murphys and he has learned to cook Irish stew.`,statements:[{text:`Hiroshi lives alone in a flat.`,answer:!1},{text:`Hiroshi has a job in the afternoons.`,answer:!0},{text:`Hiroshi finds it easy to understand fast speakers.`,answer:!1},{text:`It rains less in Dublin than in Hiroshi's home town.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-034`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'from June to September', 'including weekends', 'No experience is necessary' and 'you can eat as much ice cream as you like'.`,passage:`WANTED: Friendly and reliable people to work in our new ice cream shop on the beach this summer. The job is from June to September, and you will work four or five days a week, including weekends. No experience is necessary because we will give you training, but you must be at least sixteen years old. You should enjoy working with people and be good at maths, because you will have to handle money. We pay £9 per hour, and you can eat as much ice cream as you like! To apply, send an email with your CV to Gina.`,statements:[{text:`The job is only for the summer months.`,answer:!0},{text:`You will never work at weekends.`,answer:!1},{text:`You need to have experience to apply.`,answer:!1},{text:`Staff can eat ice cream for free.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-035`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'stop using her car for short journeys', 'he has his own small bike', 'takes about fifteen minutes' and 'She still uses the car'.`,passage:`When Kate's son Max was born, she decided to stop using her car for short journeys. She bought a bicycle with a special seat for Max and started cycling everywhere: to the shops, to the doctor's and to visit friends. Now Max is four and he has his own small bike. They cycle to his nursery together every morning, which takes about fifteen minutes. Kate says that cycling has saved her a lot of money on petrol, and she has also lost weight. She still uses the car when the weather is very bad or when she has to travel a long distance.`,statements:[{text:`Kate stopped driving short distances after her son was born.`,answer:!0},{text:`Max now has a bike of his own.`,answer:!0},{text:`The journey to the nursery takes about an hour.`,answer:!1},{text:`Kate has sold her car.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-036`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'grows in hot countries', 'their drink was bitter, not sweet', 'Solid chocolate bars were not made until the nineteenth century' and 'most of the world's cacao is grown in West Africa'.`,passage:`Chocolate comes from the seeds of the cacao tree, which grows in hot countries near the equator. People in Central America were drinking chocolate more than three thousand years ago, but their drink was bitter, not sweet. When chocolate arrived in Europe in the sixteenth century, people started adding sugar to it. Solid chocolate bars were not made until the nineteenth century. Today, most of the world's cacao is grown in West Africa, especially in Ivory Coast and Ghana. However, many cacao farmers are poor, and they earn only a small part of the money that people pay for chocolate.`,statements:[{text:`Cacao trees grow best in cold countries.`,answer:!1},{text:`The first chocolate drinks were not sweet.`,answer:!0},{text:`Chocolate bars were first made in the sixteenth century.`,answer:!1},{text:`A lot of cacao comes from West Africa.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-037`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'with her friend', 'an elderly man', 'The dog was cold but not hurt' and 'Police later warned people not to walk on the ice'.`,passage:`On Saturday afternoon, a young woman called Ellie saved a dog which had fallen through the ice on a frozen lake in Hilltop Park. Ellie was walking in the park with her friend when she heard the dog barking. The dog's owner, an elderly man, was standing by the lake and shouting for help. Ellie lay down on the ice so that she wouldn't fall through, and she pulled the dog out by its collar. The dog was cold but not hurt. Police later warned people not to walk on the ice, because it is much thinner than it looks.`,statements:[{text:`Ellie was alone in the park.`,answer:!1},{text:`The dog's owner was a young boy.`,answer:!1},{text:`The dog wasn't injured.`,answer:!0},{text:`The police said that walking on the ice was safe.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-038`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'in the main square', 'produced within forty kilometres of the town', 'sometimes a little higher than in the supermarket' and 'planning to open it on Saturdays too'.`,passage:`Our town's farmers' market takes place every Friday morning in the main square. About thirty local farmers sell fresh fruit, vegetables, eggs, cheese and bread. Everything is produced within forty kilometres of the town. The prices are sometimes a little higher than in the supermarket, but the food is fresher and tastes better. You can also talk to the farmers and ask them how the food was grown. I go every week with my daughter. Her favourite stall sells homemade apple juice. The market has become so popular that the council is planning to open it on Saturdays too.`,statements:[{text:`The market is held in the main square.`,answer:!0},{text:`All the food comes from the local area.`,answer:!0},{text:`The food at the market is always cheaper than in the supermarket.`,answer:!1},{text:`The market might open on another day as well.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-039`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'for two years', 'didn't speak any English', 'the family were very patient with her' and 'she could have long conversations and even understand jokes'.`,passage:`Nina had been learning Spanish for two years, but she still felt nervous when she had to speak it. So last summer she went on a language course in Valencia for a month. She stayed with a Spanish family who didn't speak any English, so she had to speak Spanish all the time. At first she made a lot of mistakes and felt embarrassed, but the family were very patient with her. By the end of the month, she could have long conversations and even understand jokes. Nina says it was the best way to learn a language, and she wants to go back next year.`,statements:[{text:`Nina had studied Spanish for five years.`,answer:!1},{text:`The family Nina stayed with didn't speak English.`,answer:!0},{text:`The family were impatient when Nina made mistakes.`,answer:!1},{text:`Nina's Spanish improved during the course.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-040`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'from 9 a.m. to 3 p.m.', 'in the basement', 'We suggest filling some bottles with water' and 'Mr Hughes, in flat 1'.`,passage:`Dear residents, please note that the water in the building will be turned off on Wednesday from 9 a.m. to 3 p.m. while workers replace some old pipes in the basement. During this time, you won't be able to use the taps, showers or toilets. We suggest filling some bottles with water on Tuesday evening. The lift will also be out of order on Wednesday morning, because the workers need to use it to carry equipment. We apologise for the problem and thank you for your patience. If you have any questions, please contact the building manager, Mr Hughes, in flat 1.`,statements:[{text:`The water will be off all day on Wednesday.`,answer:!1},{text:`The work will take place on the top floor.`,answer:!1},{text:`Residents are advised to keep some water in bottles.`,answer:!0},{text:`The building manager lives in flat 10.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-041`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'after he saw firefighters rescue a family', 'most of his work isn't about fires', 'visits schools to teach children about safety' and 'he sometimes sleeps at the fire station'.`,passage:`Tom is a firefighter in a small town. He joined the fire service eight years ago, after he saw firefighters rescue a family from a burning house near his home. Many people think firefighters only fight fires, but most of his work isn't about fires. He often helps people after car accidents, rescues animals and visits schools to teach children about safety. Firefighters have to be very fit, so Tom goes to the gym four times a week. He works in shifts, which means that he sometimes sleeps at the fire station. He says the best part of the job is the team spirit.`,statements:[{text:`Tom decided to become a firefighter after seeing a rescue.`,answer:!0},{text:`Most of Tom's work involves putting out fires.`,answer:!1},{text:`Tom sometimes teaches children.`,answer:!0},{text:`Tom sometimes spends the night at the fire station.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-042`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'much faster than my old one', 'my old phone always died in the afternoon', 'it doesn't fit in my jeans pocket' and 'it was worth the money'.`,passage:`Hi Sam, I hope you're well! I wanted to tell you about the new phone I bought last week. It's much faster than my old one and the camera is amazing. I took some photos of the sunset at the beach yesterday and they look professional! The battery lasts for two days, which is great because my old phone always died in the afternoon. The only problem is that it's quite big, so it doesn't fit in my jeans pocket. It was expensive, but I think it was worth the money. Have you bought a new phone yet, or are you still using your old one? Chloe`,statements:[{text:`Chloe's new phone is faster than her old one.`,answer:!0},{text:`Chloe's old phone had a better battery.`,answer:!1},{text:`The new phone fits easily in her pocket.`,answer:!1},{text:`Chloe thinks the phone was good value.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-043`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'it was finished in 2012', 'some very expensive flats', 'up to sixty-four kilometres on a clear day' and 'some people didn't like the design'.`,passage:`The Shard is one of the tallest buildings in Europe. It is in London, near London Bridge station, and it was finished in 2012. The building is 310 metres high and it has 95 floors. It contains offices, restaurants, a hotel and some very expensive flats. On the top floors there is a viewing platform, where visitors can see up to sixty-four kilometres on a clear day. The building got its name because it looks like a piece of broken glass. At first, some people didn't like the design, but now it is one of the most famous buildings in the city.`,statements:[{text:`The Shard was built in the 1990s.`,answer:!1},{text:`People live in the Shard.`,answer:!0},{text:`Visitors can only see a few kilometres from the top.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people didn't like the building at first.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-044`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'her grandmother gave her a box of cards', 'over eighty countries', 'which she organises by country' and 'her favourite ones are those that people have written on'.`,passage:`Rosa has been collecting old postcards since she was ten years old. It all started when her grandmother gave her a box of cards that she had received from friends and family in the 1950s. Now Rosa has more than two thousand postcards from over eighty countries. She keeps them in special albums, which she organises by country. Her oldest card is from 1902 and shows a street in Paris. Rosa often buys postcards at markets and online, but her favourite ones are those that people have written on, because she likes reading the messages.`,statements:[{text:`Rosa's grandmother gave her the first postcards.`,answer:!0},{text:`Rosa has postcards from about twenty countries.`,answer:!1},{text:`Rosa organises her albums by year.`,answer:!1},{text:`Rosa prefers postcards with nothing written on them.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-045`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Instead of their uniforms', 'The students won the match', 'much more than last year' and 'to buy toys and books'.`,passage:`Last Friday, students at Park Hill School held a charity day to raise money for a local children's hospital. Instead of their uniforms, students wore funny costumes and paid one pound each. There was also a cake sale, and teachers took part in a football match against the oldest students. The students won the match three goals to one. In total, the school raised £2,400, which was much more than last year. The money will be used to buy toys and books for the children's ward. The head teacher said she was very proud of everyone who took part.`,statements:[{text:`Students wore their uniforms on the charity day.`,answer:!1},{text:`The students beat the teachers at football.`,answer:!0},{text:`The school raised more money than the year before.`,answer:!0},{text:`The money will be used to buy medical equipment.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-046`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'They sold their house', 'which they repaired themselves', 'they aren't allowed to stay in the same place for longer' and 'Life on the boat is cheaper'.`,passage:`Many people dream of living on a boat, and that's exactly what Mark and Jenny decided to do three years ago. They sold their house and bought an old canal boat, which they repaired themselves. The boat has a small kitchen, a bathroom and a bedroom. They move to a new place every two weeks because they aren't allowed to stay in the same place for longer. Life on the boat is cheaper than living in a house, but it can be cold in winter. Jenny works online as a designer, while Mark writes a blog about their life on the water.`,statements:[{text:`Mark and Jenny used to live in a house.`,answer:!0},{text:`They paid someone else to repair the boat.`,answer:!1},{text:`They can stay in one place as long as they like.`,answer:!1},{text:`Living on a boat is more expensive than living in a house.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-047`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Ask your friends if they can recommend someone', 'at least two lessons a week', 'don't drink too much coffee' and 'many people don't pass their test the first time'.`,passage:`Learning to drive can be stressful, but here are some tips to help you. First, choose a good instructor. Ask your friends if they can recommend someone. Second, try to have at least two lessons a week, so that you don't forget what you've learned. You should also practise with a family member if possible, but make sure they have had a licence for several years. Before your test, get a good night's sleep and don't drink too much coffee. Finally, remember that many people don't pass their test the first time, so don't worry if you fail.`,statements:[{text:`Friends can help you find a good instructor.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer suggests having one lesson a month.`,answer:!1},{text:`You shouldn't drink too much coffee before the test.`,answer:!0},{text:`It is common to fail the test the first time.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-048`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'with his brother', 'At first they had very few customers', 'gets up at four o'clock' and 'made using his mother's recipe'.`,passage:`Ahmed runs a small bakery in a quiet street in Birmingham. He opened it five years ago with his brother, after they both lost their jobs in a factory. At first they had very few customers, but slowly people started to hear about their bread and cakes. Now there is often a queue outside the shop on Saturday mornings. Ahmed gets up at four o'clock every day to start baking. The most popular product is a sweet bread with honey and nuts, which is made using his mother's recipe. Next year the brothers are hoping to open a second shop.`,statements:[{text:`Ahmed opened the bakery on his own.`,answer:!1},{text:`The bakery wasn't busy at the beginning.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ahmed starts baking at six o'clock.`,answer:!1},{text:`The honey bread is based on his mother's recipe.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-049`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'the first in the town for more than twenty years', 'five screens', 'old classic films every Monday evening at half price' and 'Some people, however, have complained'.`,passage:`A new cinema opened in Westbridge last weekend, the first in the town for more than twenty years. The old cinema closed in 1999 because not enough people went there. The new one has five screens and very comfortable seats which you can move into a lying position. As well as new films, it will show old classic films every Monday evening at half price. There is also a café and a small restaurant. On the opening day, all the tickets were sold out by lunchtime. Some people, however, have complained that the tickets are too expensive.`,statements:[{text:`Westbridge didn't have a cinema for many years.`,answer:!0},{text:`The new cinema has only one screen.`,answer:!1},{text:`Old films are cheaper on Mondays.`,answer:!0},{text:`Nobody has complained about the cinema.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-050`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'she sails alone', 'I liked the main character', 'about four hundred pages' and 'the ending happens too quickly'.`,passage:`I've just finished reading a great book about a girl who travels around the world on a sailing boat. She's only sixteen, but she sails alone for nine months. The story is exciting, especially when she gets caught in a terrible storm in the Pacific Ocean. I liked the main character because she is brave but also honest about her fears. The book is quite long, about four hundred pages, but it's easy to read. My only criticism is that the ending happens too quickly. I would recommend it to anyone who likes adventure stories. I've already lent it to my cousin.`,statements:[{text:`The girl in the book sails with her father.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer liked the main character.`,answer:!0},{text:`The book is very short.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer liked the ending very much.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-051`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'for twelve years', 'seven and eight years old', 'she has to mark books and plan lessons in the evening' and 'The children are still talking about it'.`,passage:`Grace has been a primary school teacher for twelve years. She teaches a class of twenty-eight children who are seven and eight years old. Her day starts at eight o'clock, when she prepares the classroom, and lessons finish at three. However, her work doesn't end then, because she has to mark books and plan lessons in the evening. Grace says that the best part of her job is seeing children learn something new. Last year she took her class on a trip to a farm, where they learned how to milk a cow. The children are still talking about it.`,statements:[{text:`Grace has been teaching for twenty years.`,answer:!1},{text:`Grace's pupils are seven and eight years old.`,answer:!0},{text:`Grace works in the evenings too.`,answer:!0},{text:`The children enjoyed the farm trip.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-052`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'two hundred metres from a beautiful sandy beach', 'perfect for a family of four', 'Pets are welcome' and 'The nearest shop is in the village, about two kilometres away'.`,passage:`Are you looking for a quiet place for your holiday? Then come to Sea View Cottage, a small stone house just two hundred metres from a beautiful sandy beach. The cottage has two bedrooms, so it is perfect for a family of four. There is a fully equipped kitchen, a garden with a barbecue and free wifi. Pets are welcome, but please tell us before you arrive. The nearest shop is in the village, about two kilometres away, so you will need a car. The cottage is available from April to October. Prices start at £450 per week.`,statements:[{text:`The cottage is close to the beach.`,answer:!0},{text:`The cottage is suitable for four people.`,answer:!0},{text:`Pets are not allowed in the cottage.`,answer:!1},{text:`There is a shop next to the cottage.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-053`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'I helped her feed the chickens', 'There was no television at the farm', 'I never felt bored' and 'My aunt sold the farm ten years ago'.`,passage:`When I was a child, I used to spend every summer at my aunt's farm in the countryside. I helped her feed the chickens every morning and collect the eggs. In the afternoons, my cousins and I swam in the river or climbed trees. There was no television at the farm, so in the evenings we played cards or listened to my uncle's stories. I didn't have a phone then, of course, but I never felt bored. My aunt sold the farm ten years ago and moved to the city. I sometimes drive past it, but it looks very different now.`,statements:[{text:`The writer helped with the chickens.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer watched television every evening at the farm.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer often felt bored on the farm.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer's aunt doesn't live on the farm any more.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-054`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'it can stay for hundreds of years', 'they think they are food', 'shops have to charge customers for plastic bags' and 'use a metal water bottle'.`,passage:`Plastic is a big problem for our oceans. Every year, millions of tonnes of plastic end up in the sea, where it can stay for hundreds of years. Sea animals such as turtles and birds sometimes eat plastic bags because they think they are food. Many countries have now introduced rules to reduce plastic use. For example, in some places shops have to charge customers for plastic bags. You can help too: carry a reusable bag when you go shopping, use a metal water bottle and try to buy products which don't have much packaging.`,statements:[{text:`Plastic disappears from the sea after a few months.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some sea animals eat plastic by mistake.`,answer:!0},{text:`In some countries, people must pay for plastic bags.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer suggests buying more bottled water.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-055`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'one of the books you ordered... is out of stock', 'The other two books', 'were sent this morning' and 'give you your money back'.`,passage:`Dear Customer, thank you for ordering from Bookworld. We are sorry to tell you that one of the books you ordered, 'The Silent Forest', is out of stock at the moment. We expect to receive more copies in about three weeks. The other two books in your order were sent this morning and should arrive in two or three working days. You can choose to wait for 'The Silent Forest', or we can cancel it and give you your money back. Please reply to this email to tell us what you would prefer. We apologise for the delay. Kind regards, Bookworld Customer Service`,statements:[{text:`All the books in the order are out of stock.`,answer:!1},{text:`The customer ordered four books.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some of the books have already been sent.`,answer:!0},{text:`The customer can ask for a refund.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-056`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'every day except Sunday', 'he started playing football when he was five', 'A coach... invited him to join the club' and 'he is also studying sports science online'.`,passage:`Leo is nineteen and he is training to become a professional footballer. He plays for the youth team of a big club in the north of England. He trains every day except Sunday, and he also has to watch what he eats very carefully. Leo started playing football when he was five, in a park near his house. A coach saw him play when he was eleven and invited him to join the club. Leo knows that only a few young players get a professional contract, so he is also studying sports science online, in case his football career doesn't work out.`,statements:[{text:`Leo trains six days a week.`,answer:!0},{text:`Leo started playing football at the age of eleven.`,answer:!1},{text:`A coach invited Leo to join the club.`,answer:!0},{text:`Leo is studying as well as playing football.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-057`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'green and purple lights', 'between September and March', 'easier to see away from towns' and 'they don't appear every night'.`,passage:`Thousands of people visit Iceland every year to see the northern lights. These beautiful green and purple lights appear in the night sky when particles from the sun hit the Earth's atmosphere. The best time to see them is between September and March, when the nights are long and dark. You need a clear sky, so it's a good idea to check the weather forecast before you go out. The lights are easier to see away from towns, where there are no street lights. However, nobody can promise that you will see them, because they don't appear every night.`,statements:[{text:`The lights can be green and purple.`,answer:!0},{text:`The best time to see the lights is in summer.`,answer:!1},{text:`It's easier to see the lights in the town centre.`,answer:!1},{text:`The lights appear every night.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-058`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'I had forgotten mine', 'she went to university in Scotland while I stayed in London', 'Now she lives in Canada' and 'we talk on video calls every week'.`,passage:`My best friend Zoe and I met on our first day at primary school, when we were both five. We sat next to each other and she lent me a pencil because I had forgotten mine. Since then, we've been friends for more than twenty years. We went to the same secondary school, but then she went to university in Scotland while I stayed in London. Now she lives in Canada with her husband, so we only see each other once a year. However, we talk on video calls every week, and she still makes me laugh more than anyone else.`,statements:[{text:`The writer had forgotten her pencil on the first day.`,answer:!0},{text:`Zoe and the writer went to the same university.`,answer:!1},{text:`Zoe lives in Scotland now.`,answer:!1},{text:`The two friends talk every week.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-059`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'skating in the car park behind the supermarket', 'wrote a letter to the town council asking for a safe place to skate', 'will be built next to the sports centre' and 'The teenagers will help to choose the design'.`,passage:`The town of Greenfield is going to build a new skate park for young people. For years, teenagers have been skating in the car park behind the supermarket, which is dangerous because of the cars. Last year, a group of teenagers wrote a letter to the town council asking for a safe place to skate. They also collected more than one thousand signatures. The council agreed, and the new park will be built next to the sports centre. It will cost £200,000 and should be ready by next summer. The teenagers will help to choose the design.`,statements:[{text:`Teenagers have been skating in a car park.`,answer:!0},{text:`The teenagers asked the council for a skate park.`,answer:!0},{text:`The skate park will be built behind the supermarket.`,answer:!1},{text:`The teenagers will help with the design.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-060`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'In the afternoon it started to rain', 'we went to a museum instead', 'which was really funny' and 'our room was really small'.`,passage:`Hi Anna, I've just got back from my weekend in Edinburgh and I had a great time! On Saturday morning we walked up to the castle, which has amazing views of the city. In the afternoon it started to rain, so we went to a museum instead of walking around. On Saturday evening we went to a small theatre to see a comedy show, which was really funny. On Sunday the weather was much better, so we climbed a hill called Arthur's Seat. My legs still hurt! The only bad thing was the hotel, because our room was really small. You should go one day!`,statements:[{text:`It was sunny all weekend.`,answer:!1},{text:`They visited a museum because of the rain.`,answer:!0},{text:`The comedy show wasn't very funny.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer liked the hotel room.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-061`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'make a list before you go shopping', 'restaurant meals are much more expensive', 'cancel any subscriptions that you don't really use' and 'every time you get paid, put a small amount of money into a savings account before you spend anything'.`,passage:`Many people find it hard to save money, but a few small changes can help. Firstly, make a list before you go shopping and only buy what is on it. Secondly, try cooking at home instead of eating out, because restaurant meals are much more expensive. You could also take a packed lunch to work or school. Another idea is to cancel any subscriptions that you don't really use, such as a gym membership or a TV service. Finally, every time you get paid, put a small amount of money into a savings account before you spend anything.`,statements:[{text:`The writer suggests making a shopping list.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer says eating out is cheaper than cooking.`,answer:!1},{text:`You could save money by cancelling services you don't use.`,answer:!0},{text:`You should save money only at the end of the month.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-062`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'for the first time', 'showed her how to send emails and make video calls', 'her son, who lives in Australia' and 'She has even started doing her shopping online'.`,passage:`Ruth is seventy-two, and last year she learned to use the internet for the first time. Her granddaughter gave her a tablet for her birthday and showed her how to send emails and make video calls. At first Ruth found it confusing, but she practised every day. Now she uses the tablet to read the news, look up recipes and talk to her son, who lives in Australia. She has even started doing her shopping online, so she doesn't have to carry heavy bags home. Ruth says she wishes she had learned to use the internet years ago.`,statements:[{text:`Ruth has used the internet for many years.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ruth's granddaughter taught her how to use the tablet.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ruth's son lives abroad.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ruth still carries all her shopping home herself.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-063`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'eating flat bread with toppings hundreds of years ago', 'in Naples, in the south of Italy', 'cheap food for poor people' and 'after many Italians moved there'.`,passage:`Pizza is one of the most popular foods in the world, but it has a long history. People in many countries were eating flat bread with toppings hundreds of years ago. However, the modern pizza with tomato sauce was first made in Naples, in the south of Italy, in the eighteenth century. At that time it was cheap food for poor people, who bought it in the street. Pizza became popular in the USA in the twentieth century, after many Italians moved there. Today, the most popular pizza in many countries is the simple margherita, with tomato, cheese and basil.`,statements:[{text:`People ate flat bread with toppings a long time ago.`,answer:!0},{text:`Modern pizza was first made in the north of Italy.`,answer:!1},{text:`In the past, pizza was food for rich people.`,answer:!1},{text:`Pizza became popular in the USA after Italians moved there.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-064`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Your working day starts at 8.30 a.m.', 'a canteen on the second floor', 'places are limited' and 'you must call your manager'.`,passage:`Please read the following information before you start your new job. Your working day starts at 8.30 a.m., and you should arrive ten minutes early on your first day so that we can give you your ID card. Lunch is from 12.30 to 1.30 p.m., and there is a canteen on the second floor which serves hot meals. Staff can park in the car park behind the building, but places are limited, so we recommend taking public transport. If you are ill and can't come to work, you must call your manager before 9 a.m. We hope you enjoy working with us.`,statements:[{text:`The working day starts at 8.20 a.m.`,answer:!1},{text:`The canteen is on the second floor.`,answer:!0},{text:`There aren't many parking places.`,answer:!0},{text:`You should send an email if you are ill.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-065`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'had never been interested in art', 'he was surprised to find that he really enjoyed it', 'put it on the wall in their kitchen' and 'he is thinking of selling some of them'.`,passage:`Jack had never been interested in art until his girlfriend took him to a painting class for his birthday. He thought it would be boring, but he was surprised to find that he really enjoyed it. The teacher showed them how to paint a simple landscape with mountains and a lake. Jack's painting wasn't perfect, but his girlfriend liked it so much that she put it on the wall in their kitchen. Since then, Jack has been going to the class every Wednesday evening. He has painted about twenty pictures, and he is thinking of selling some of them at a local market.`,statements:[{text:`Jack had always been interested in art.`,answer:!1},{text:`Jack enjoyed the first class more than he expected.`,answer:!0},{text:`Jack's first painting is in the living room.`,answer:!1},{text:`Jack might sell some of his paintings.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-066`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'has grown a lot in recent years', 'Chickens are quite easy to look after', 'about five eggs a week' and 'they can be noisy in the morning'.`,passage:`The number of people who keep chickens in their gardens has grown a lot in recent years. Chickens are quite easy to look after, as long as they have a safe place to sleep at night, fresh water and food. A healthy chicken can lay about five eggs a week. Many families say that the eggs taste much better than the ones they buy in shops. Chickens also eat insects and some kitchen waste, which is good for the garden. However, before you buy chickens, you should check that your neighbours don't mind, because they can be noisy in the morning.`,statements:[{text:`More people are keeping chickens than before.`,answer:!0},{text:`Chickens are very difficult to look after.`,answer:!1},{text:`A healthy chicken can lay several eggs a week.`,answer:!0},{text:`Chickens can make noise early in the day.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-067`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'nearly five hours', 'just when I was cooking dinner', 'played board games by candlelight' and 'we were almost disappointed'.`,passage:`Last night, there was a power cut in our part of the city which lasted for nearly five hours. It started at about seven o'clock, just when I was cooking dinner. Luckily, I had some candles in the kitchen drawer. Because I couldn't use the cooker, I made sandwiches instead. My phone battery was low, so I couldn't use it much. In the end, my family and I sat together and played board games by candlelight, which we hadn't done for years. When the lights came back on at midnight, we were almost disappointed!`,statements:[{text:`The power cut lasted about an hour.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer was cooking when the power cut started.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer's family watched TV during the power cut.`,answer:!1},{text:`The family were happy when the lights came back on.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-068`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'learn the names of thousands of streets', 'nearly four years', 'drove around the city on a motorbike' and 'Fatima rarely needs one'.`,passage:`Fatima is a taxi driver in London. To get her licence, she had to learn the names of thousands of streets and the quickest ways to go from one place to another. This took her nearly four years, and she had to pass several difficult tests. She says that she drove around the city on a motorbike for hours every day to learn the roads. Most London taxi drivers today use a satellite navigation system, but Fatima rarely needs one. She enjoys meeting people from all over the world, although some passengers can be rude.`,statements:[{text:`Fatima had to learn a lot of street names.`,answer:!0},{text:`Fatima got her licence in a few months.`,answer:!1},{text:`Fatima used a motorbike to learn the roads.`,answer:!0},{text:`Fatima uses satellite navigation on every journey.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-069`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'on the first Thursday of every month', 'all kinds of books', 'you don't have to finish the book' and 'Membership is free'.`,passage:`Come and join the Brookside Book Club! We meet on the first Thursday of every month at 7 p.m. in the back room of the Red Lion café. Every month we choose a different book to read, and then we meet to talk about it. We read all kinds of books, from crime stories to history and travel writing. New members are always welcome, and you don't have to finish the book before you come. Membership is free, but please buy a drink at the café to thank them for letting us use the room. Next month's book is 'A Winter in Norway'.`,statements:[{text:`The club meets every Thursday.`,answer:!1},{text:`The club reads different kinds of books.`,answer:!0},{text:`You must finish the book before the meeting.`,answer:!1},{text:`The club doesn't charge members.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-070`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'to raise money for a cancer charity', 'Sometimes he slept in a tent... people often invited him to stay in their homes', 'almost a year' and 'which became a bestseller'.`,passage:`In 2015, a man called Peter decided to walk around the whole coast of Britain to raise money for a cancer charity. His mother had died of cancer the year before. He started in London and walked about twenty-five kilometres a day, carrying everything he needed in a big backpack. Sometimes he slept in a tent, but people often invited him to stay in their homes. The walk took him almost a year. Peter raised more than £100,000 for the charity, and he later wrote a book about his journey, which became a bestseller.`,statements:[{text:`Peter walked to raise money for charity.`,answer:!0},{text:`Peter always slept in hotels.`,answer:!1},{text:`The walk took nearly twelve months.`,answer:!0},{text:`Peter's book sold very well.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-071`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'the forecast says it's going to be cold and rainy', 'It starts at seven, not eight', 'there'll be pizza and chips' and 'My parents are paying for the first two games'.`,passage:`Hi Lucas, are you still coming to my birthday party on Friday? There's been a change of plan. We were going to have it in the garden, but the forecast says it's going to be cold and rainy, so we've decided to have it at the bowling alley in Hill Street instead. It starts at seven, not eight as I said before. Don't worry about food because there'll be pizza and chips. My parents are paying for the first two games, but if you want to play more, you'll have to pay for yourself. Can you bring your sister too? Mia`,statements:[{text:`The party has moved because of the weather.`,answer:!0},{text:`The party will now start at eight.`,answer:!1},{text:`Guests should bring their own food.`,answer:!1},{text:`Guests can play as many free games as they like.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-072`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'more than fifty countries', 'Brazil produces the most coffee in the world', 'the seeds of a red fruit called a coffee cherry' and 'too much coffee can make it difficult to sleep'.`,passage:`Coffee is grown in more than fifty countries, but Brazil produces the most coffee in the world. Coffee plants need warm weather and lots of rain, and they usually grow in mountain areas. The coffee beans are actually the seeds of a red fruit called a coffee cherry. After they are picked, the seeds are dried and then roasted, which gives coffee its brown colour and strong smell. Some people drink several cups a day because it helps them stay awake. However, doctors say that too much coffee can make it difficult to sleep and can make some people feel nervous.`,statements:[{text:`Coffee is grown in fewer than ten countries.`,answer:!1},{text:`Brazil is the biggest coffee producer.`,answer:!0},{text:`Coffee beans come from a red fruit.`,answer:!0},{text:`Doctors say you can drink as much coffee as you like.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-073`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'He started swimming when he was a young sailor in the navy', 'he walks to the public swimming pool', 'he sometimes swims in the sea' and 'he won a medal'.`,passage:`My neighbour, Mr Brown, is eighty-five and he still goes swimming every morning. He started swimming when he was a young sailor in the navy, more than sixty years ago. Every day at seven o'clock, he walks to the public swimming pool, which is about a kilometre from his house, and swims thirty lengths. In summer, he sometimes swims in the sea instead. He says that swimming keeps his body strong and his mind clear. Last year, he won a medal in a swimming competition for people over eighty. His doctor says he is healthier than many people half his age.`,statements:[{text:`Mr Brown learned to swim in the navy.`,answer:!0},{text:`Mr Brown drives to the swimming pool.`,answer:!1},{text:`Mr Brown sometimes swims in the sea.`,answer:!0},{text:`Mr Brown has won a swimming medal.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-074`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'rent electric scooters using an app on their phones', 'they don't produce pollution', 'Some people leave them on the pavement' and 'In some cities... they cannot ride on the pavement'.`,passage:`In many cities, people can now rent electric scooters using an app on their phones. You simply find a scooter in the street, scan the code and start riding. When you finish, you leave the scooter in a special parking area. Scooters are cheap and fast, and they don't produce pollution. However, they are not popular with everyone. Some people leave them on the pavement, where they block the way for people walking. There have also been accidents, because some riders go too fast. In some cities, riders now have to wear helmets and they cannot ride on the pavement.`,statements:[{text:`You use a phone app to rent the scooters.`,answer:!0},{text:`The scooters produce a lot of pollution.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people leave scooters in the way of pedestrians.`,answer:!0},{text:`In all cities, riders can ride on the pavement.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-075`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'He takes groups of tourists around the city's most famous places', 'English, Italian, Spanish and German', 'he fell in love with the city during a holiday' and 'the hardest part of the job is the heat in summer'.`,passage:`Simon works as a tour guide in Rome. He takes groups of tourists around the city's most famous places, such as the Colosseum and the Trevi Fountain. He speaks four languages: English, Italian, Spanish and German. Simon grew up in London, but he moved to Rome fifteen years ago after he fell in love with the city during a holiday. He says that the hardest part of the job is the heat in summer, when it can be over thirty-five degrees. His favourite moment of every tour is when tourists see the Pantheon for the first time, because they always look amazed.`,statements:[{text:`Simon shows tourists famous places in Rome.`,answer:!0},{text:`Simon can speak German.`,answer:!0},{text:`Simon visited Rome on holiday before he moved there.`,answer:!0},{text:`Simon finds the summer weather easy to work in.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-076`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'organised by a local environmental group', 'lasted four hours', 'some had been carried in by the sea' and 'especially the many families with young children'.`,passage:`Last Saturday, about fifty volunteers met on Silver Beach to pick up rubbish. The event was organised by a local environmental group and lasted four hours. The volunteers collected more than two hundred bags of rubbish, including plastic bottles, fishing nets, and even an old bicycle. The organisers said that most of the rubbish had been left by visitors in the summer, but some had been carried in by the sea. They were very pleased with the number of people who took part, especially the many families with young children. The group is planning to hold another clean-up in the spring.`,statements:[{text:`The clean-up was organised by the town council.`,answer:!1},{text:`The volunteers worked for the whole day.`,answer:!1},{text:`All the rubbish was left by visitors.`,answer:!1},{text:`Many families took part in the event.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-077`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'I fell off my bike', 'Luckily it isn't broken', 'I shouldn't play any sport for at least two weeks' and 'his phone is always switched off'.`,passage:`Hi Rob, I'm afraid I can't come to football practice on Thursday. I fell off my bike on Sunday and hurt my wrist. I went to the hospital and they took an X-ray. Luckily it isn't broken, but the doctor said I shouldn't play any sport for at least two weeks. It's really annoying because we've got the big match against Westfield at the end of the month. I hope I'll be able to play in that. Could you tell the coach for me? I've tried to call him, but his phone is always switched off. Thanks, Danny`,statements:[{text:`Danny had an accident on his bike.`,answer:!0},{text:`Danny's wrist is not broken.`,answer:!0},{text:`Danny can play sport again next week.`,answer:!1},{text:`Danny hasn't been able to speak to the coach.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-078`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'lives in the mountains', 'up to fourteen hours a day eating', 'pink with no fur' and 'the number of wild pandas has increased'.`,passage:`The giant panda lives in the mountains of central China. Pandas eat mainly bamboo, and an adult panda can spend up to fourteen hours a day eating. Because bamboo doesn't have much energy, pandas move slowly and sleep a lot. Baby pandas are very small when they are born, about the size of a stick of butter, and they are pink with no fur. For many years, the panda was in danger of disappearing because people cut down the forests where it lives. Thanks to the work of the Chinese government and conservation groups, the number of wild pandas has increased.`,statements:[{text:`Pandas live in the deserts of China.`,answer:!1},{text:`Pandas spend very little time eating.`,answer:!1},{text:`Baby pandas have no fur when they are born.`,answer:!0},{text:`There are fewer wild pandas now than in the past.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-079`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'three years ago', 'she had worked in a large clothes factory', 'young people who want to buy fewer new clothes to help the environment' and 'she teaches people to sew'.`,passage:`Jenny opened a small shop that repairs clothes three years ago. Before that, she had worked in a large clothes factory for many years. She noticed that people were throwing away clothes just because a button was missing or a zip was broken. Now she repairs jackets, trousers and dresses, and she can also make clothes shorter or longer. Many of her customers are young people who want to buy fewer new clothes to help the environment. Jenny also runs evening classes where she teaches people to sew. She says that everyone should know how to sew on a button.`,statements:[{text:`Jenny has had her shop for ten years.`,answer:!1},{text:`Jenny used to work in a factory.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some of her customers want to help the environment.`,answer:!0},{text:`Jenny teaches sewing classes.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-080`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'You won't need to look after the animals', 'You must be at least eighteen', 'Full training will be given' and 'free entry to the zoo for themselves and one friend'.`,passage:`Westgate Zoo is looking for volunteers to help on weekends. Volunteers will help visitors to find their way around the zoo, answer simple questions about the animals and help with children's activities. You won't need to look after the animals, as this is done by our trained keepers. You must be at least eighteen and able to work at least two weekends a month. Full training will be given. In return, volunteers get free entry to the zoo for themselves and one friend, and a discount in the zoo café. If you are interested, please fill in the form on our website.`,statements:[{text:`Volunteers will feed and look after the animals.`,answer:!1},{text:`Sixteen-year-olds can become volunteers.`,answer:!1},{text:`The zoo will train the volunteers.`,answer:!0},{text:`Volunteers can bring a friend to the zoo for free.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-081`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'his English was quite basic', 'He found a job washing dishes', 'After two years, the head chef gave him a job as a cook' and 'he now employs twelve people'.`,passage:`When Carlos arrived in London from Colombia, he didn't know anyone and his English was quite basic. He found a job washing dishes in a hotel kitchen, and in the evenings he went to English classes. The hours were long and the job was tiring, but he watched the chefs carefully and asked them lots of questions. After two years, the head chef gave him a job as a cook. Ten years later, Carlos opened his own restaurant serving Colombian food. It has become one of the most popular restaurants in the area, and he now employs twelve people.`,statements:[{text:`Carlos didn't speak much English when he arrived.`,answer:!0},{text:`Carlos's first job was washing dishes.`,answer:!0},{text:`Carlos became a cook after a few weeks.`,answer:!1},{text:`Carlos works alone in his restaurant.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-082`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'not drinking enough water', 'more when it is hot or when you do sport', 'as can stress' and 'If the headaches don't stop, you should see a doctor'.`,passage:`Many people get headaches, and there are often simple reasons for them. One of the most common causes is not drinking enough water. Doctors recommend drinking about two litres of water a day, and more when it is hot or when you do sport. Looking at a computer screen for many hours without a break can also cause headaches, as can stress and lack of sleep. If you often get headaches, try to take short breaks from your screen, go for a walk in the fresh air and go to bed earlier. If the headaches don't stop, you should see a doctor.`,statements:[{text:`Drinking too much water is a common cause of headaches.`,answer:!1},{text:`You should drink more water when you do sport.`,answer:!0},{text:`Stress can cause headaches.`,answer:!0},{text:`You should see a doctor as soon as you get a headache.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-083`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'advertised in the window', 'studying literature', 'I am used to dealing with customers' and 'weekday afternoons after two o'clock'.`,passage:`Dear Sir or Madam, I would like to apply for the job of sales assistant at your bookshop, which I saw advertised in the window last week. I am twenty years old and I am studying literature at the local college. I have worked part-time in a supermarket for two years, so I am used to dealing with customers and working with money. I love reading, especially novels and poetry, and I think I could give customers good advice. I am available to work on Saturdays and on weekday afternoons after two o'clock. I look forward to hearing from you. Yours faithfully, Karen Lee`,statements:[{text:`Karen saw the job advert in the shop window.`,answer:!0},{text:`Karen is studying history.`,answer:!1},{text:`Karen has experience of working with customers.`,answer:!0},{text:`Karen can work on weekday mornings.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-084`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'every July', 'over high mountains', 'The rider with the lowest total time wears a yellow shirt' and 'it has only been cancelled during the two world wars'.`,passage:`The Tour de France is the most famous bicycle race in the world. It takes place every July, and it lasts about three weeks. The riders cycle about three and a half thousand kilometres, through flat countryside and over high mountains. The race is divided into twenty-one stages, one for each day, with two rest days. The rider with the lowest total time wears a yellow shirt. The first race was held in 1903, and it has only been cancelled during the two world wars. Millions of people watch the race on TV, and thousands stand by the road to cheer the riders.`,statements:[{text:`The race takes place in the summer.`,answer:!0},{text:`The race goes through mountains.`,answer:!0},{text:`The leader wears a yellow shirt.`,answer:!0},{text:`The race has never been cancelled.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-085`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'except food and medicine', 'It was harder than we expected', 'we had to find second-hand ones online' and 'We are going to try it again this year'.`,passage:`Last year my family and I decided to spend a whole month without buying anything new, except food and medicine. It was harder than we expected. In the first week, my son's school shoes broke, so we had to find second-hand ones online. We also couldn't buy birthday presents, so we made them ourselves. My daughter painted a picture for her friend, and I baked a cake for my sister. At the end of the month, we had saved about £400. More importantly, we realised that we didn't need most of the things we usually buy. We are going to try it again this year.`,statements:[{text:`The family stopped buying food for a month.`,answer:!1},{text:`The experiment was easier than they expected.`,answer:!1},{text:`They bought new shoes for the son.`,answer:!1},{text:`The family plan to repeat the experiment.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-086`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'a scientist who studies whales', 'for three months every year', 'whales communicate with each other using songs' and 'sometimes she doesn't see a whale for days'.`,passage:`Hannah is a scientist who studies whales. She works on a research boat off the coast of Norway for three months every year. Her job is to count the whales and record the sounds they make, using special microphones under the water. She says that whales communicate with each other using songs, and that each group has its own song. The work can be hard because the sea is often rough and cold, and sometimes she doesn't see a whale for days. But when she does see one, she says it is the most exciting feeling in the world.`,statements:[{text:`Hannah studies dolphins.`,answer:!1},{text:`Hannah works on the boat all year.`,answer:!1},{text:`Whales use songs to communicate.`,answer:!0},{text:`Hannah sees whales every day.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-087`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'every house will get three bins', 'a green one for food waste', 'the black bin will only be collected every two weeks' and 'you will still have to take bottles and jars to the bottle bank'.`,passage:`Our town has just started a new recycling system. From next month, every house will get three bins: a green one for food waste, a blue one for paper, plastic and metal, and a black one for everything else. The green and blue bins will be collected every week, but the black bin will only be collected every two weeks. The council hopes that this will encourage people to recycle more. Glass is not included, so you will still have to take bottles and jars to the bottle bank in the supermarket car park. Old bins should be left outside for the council to collect.`,statements:[{text:`Each house will get three bins.`,answer:!0},{text:`Food waste goes in the green bin.`,answer:!0},{text:`The black bin will be collected every week.`,answer:!1},{text:`People must take glass to the bottle bank.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-088`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'since she was a little girl', 'at fifteen she got a small part in a TV series', 'she often doesn't get the part' and 'she works in a café three days a week'.`,passage:`Ella has wanted to be an actor since she was a little girl. At the age of eight, she joined a drama club at school, and at fifteen she got a small part in a TV series. Now she is twenty-two and she has just finished drama school. Life as a young actor isn't easy. She goes to lots of auditions, but she often doesn't get the part. To pay the bills, she works in a café three days a week. Next month, however, she is going to appear in a play at a theatre in Manchester. It's her biggest role so far.`,statements:[{text:`Ella decided to become an actor when she was twenty.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ella appeared in a TV series as a teenager.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ella often fails to get the parts she tries for.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ella has a part-time job in a café.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-089`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'thank you so much for the money', 'my old ones had holes in them', 'I managed to climb to the top of the highest wall' and 'a cake that Dad had made'.`,passage:`Hi Grandma, thank you so much for the money you sent for my birthday! I used it to buy a new pair of trainers, which I needed because my old ones had holes in them. I had a lovely birthday. On Saturday, Mum and Dad took me and three friends to a climbing centre, and then we went for a burger. I managed to climb to the top of the highest wall, although I was quite scared! In the evening we had a cake that Dad had made. It was chocolate, my favourite. I hope you can come and visit us soon. Lots of love, Freddie`,statements:[{text:`Grandma sent Freddie a pair of trainers.`,answer:!1},{text:`Freddie's old trainers were in good condition.`,answer:!1},{text:`Freddie climbed the highest wall.`,answer:!0},{text:`Freddie's dad made the birthday cake.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-090`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'The first bicycles had no pedals', 'fast but dangerous', 'appeared in the 1880s' and 'it was the first time they could travel easily outside their town'.`,passage:`The bicycle was invented in Europe in the early nineteenth century. The first bicycles had no pedals, so riders had to push themselves along with their feet. Later, pedals were added to the front wheel. In the 1870s, some bicycles had a very large front wheel and a tiny back wheel, which made them fast but dangerous. The modern bicycle, with two wheels of the same size and a chain, appeared in the 1880s. It quickly became popular because it was cheap and easy to ride. For many working people, it was the first time they could travel easily outside their town.`,statements:[{text:`The first bicycles had pedals on the back wheel.`,answer:!1},{text:`Bicycles with a large front wheel were very safe.`,answer:!1},{text:`The modern bicycle appeared in the 1880s.`,answer:!0},{text:`Bicycles helped working people to travel further.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-091`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'Every year in April', 'from all over Spain', 'learn how to grow vegetables on a balcony' and 'slightly fewer than last year'.`,passage:`Every year in April, the city of Valencia holds a big flower show in its main park. This year, more than one hundred gardeners from all over Spain showed their flowers and plants. The biggest attraction was a garden made to look like a small village, with houses made entirely of roses. There were also workshops where visitors could learn how to grow vegetables on a balcony. The show was open for five days and attracted about eighty thousand visitors, slightly fewer than last year because of the rain. The prize for the best garden went to a family from Seville.`,statements:[{text:`The flower show takes place every spring.`,answer:!0},{text:`All the gardeners came from Valencia.`,answer:!1},{text:`Visitors could learn about growing vegetables.`,answer:!0},{text:`More people visited the show than last year.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-092`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'about five hundred sheep', 'he sometimes works through the night', 'Ian learned everything from his father' and 'His daughter wants to be a farmer too'.`,passage:`Ian is a farmer in the north of Scotland. He keeps about five hundred sheep on a large farm in the hills. His day starts at six o'clock in the morning, and in spring, when the baby lambs are born, he sometimes works through the night. The farm has been in his family for four generations, and Ian learned everything from his father. He has two dogs that help him to move the sheep from one field to another. Ian says farming is hard work and doesn't pay very well, but he couldn't imagine doing anything else. His daughter wants to be a farmer too.`,statements:[{text:`Ian keeps cows on his farm.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ian sometimes works at night in spring.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ian's father taught him about farming.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ian's daughter is interested in farming.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-093`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'since Monday', 'the doctor has told her to stay at home until Friday', 'a science test on Thursday' and 'send me the homework by email'.`,passage:`Hello Mr Clarke, I'm writing about my daughter, Amy, who is in your Year 7 class. Unfortunately, Amy has been ill with a bad cold since Monday, and the doctor has told her to stay at home until Friday. I know that she has a science test on Thursday. Would it be possible for her to take the test next week instead? She is also worried about missing her homework. Could you please send me the homework by email so that she can do it at home if she feels better? Thank you very much for your help. Best regards, Laura Hill`,statements:[{text:`Amy has been ill since the beginning of the week.`,answer:!0},{text:`The doctor said Amy should stay at home.`,answer:!0},{text:`Amy's science test is on Friday.`,answer:!1},{text:`Laura wants the homework sent by post.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-094`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'hot liquid rock, called lava', 'others have been quiet for hundreds of years', 'many people live near volcanoes' and 'they can sometimes warn people before an eruption'.`,passage:`Volcanoes are openings in the Earth's surface where hot liquid rock, called lava, comes out. There are about fifteen hundred active volcanoes in the world, and many of them are around the edge of the Pacific Ocean. Some volcanoes erupt often, while others have been quiet for hundreds of years. Although they can be dangerous, many people live near volcanoes because the soil there is very good for growing food. Scientists study volcanoes carefully, and they can sometimes warn people before an eruption, so that they have time to leave the area.`,statements:[{text:`Lava is hot liquid rock.`,answer:!0},{text:`All volcanoes erupt very often.`,answer:!1},{text:`Nobody lives near volcanoes because they are dangerous.`,answer:!1},{text:`Scientists can sometimes warn people before an eruption.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-095`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'he got out of breath when he climbed the stairs', 'His doctor told him that he had to change his lifestyle', 'he started walking for thirty minutes every day' and 'has run three marathons'.`,passage:`Five years ago, Martin weighed over a hundred and twenty kilos and he got out of breath when he climbed the stairs. His doctor told him that he had to change his lifestyle. So he started walking for thirty minutes every day and stopped eating fast food. After six months, he started running, and a year later he ran his first race. Since then he has lost forty kilos and has run three marathons. Martin now works as a personal trainer, helping other people to get fit. He says the most important thing is to start slowly and not give up.`,statements:[{text:`Martin was very fit five years ago.`,answer:!1},{text:`Martin's doctor told him to make changes.`,answer:!0},{text:`Martin began by running every day.`,answer:!1},{text:`Martin has never run a marathon.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-096`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'children aged eight to twelve', 'then they will eat it together', 'All ingredients and aprons are provided' and 'Places are limited to ten children per class'.`,passage:`NEW: Saturday morning cooking classes for children aged eight to twelve at the Food Studio, 25 Market Street. In each class, children will learn to make a simple, healthy meal, such as vegetable soup, fresh pasta or fish cakes, and then they will eat it together. All ingredients and aprons are provided. Classes start at 10 a.m. and finish at 12. Parents don't need to stay, but they must collect their children on time. Each class costs £15. Please tell us if your child has any food allergies when you book. Places are limited to ten children per class.`,statements:[{text:`The classes are for teenagers.`,answer:!1},{text:`Children eat the food they make.`,answer:!0},{text:`Children have to bring their own ingredients.`,answer:!1},{text:`Only ten children can join each class.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-097`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'some are more than eighty years old', 'usually when they are broken', 'there are radios everywhere in the house' and 'asked to borrow some of them'.`,passage:`My dad has a strange hobby: he collects old radios. He has about sixty of them, and some are more than eighty years old. He buys them at markets, in second-hand shops and online, usually when they are broken. Then he spends hours in the garage repairing them. My mum sometimes complains because there are radios everywhere in the house, even in the bathroom! Last year, a local museum asked to borrow some of them for an exhibition about the history of radio. Dad was so proud that he visited the exhibition five times.`,statements:[{text:`Some of the radios are very old.`,answer:!0},{text:`Dad usually buys radios that don't work.`,answer:!0},{text:`All the radios are kept in the garage.`,answer:!1},{text:`Dad sold some radios to the museum.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-098`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'The last one was maths', 'We'll get our results in August', 'work at my uncle's hotel' and 'we definitely want to visit Prague and Vienna'.`,passage:`Hi Jess, how are things? I've finally finished my exams! The last one was maths, and I think it went quite well, although the last question was really difficult. We'll get our results in August. Now I'm planning my summer. In July I'm going to work at my uncle's hotel on the coast, so I can save some money. Then in August I'm going travelling around Europe by train with Katie for three weeks. We haven't decided exactly where to go yet, but we definitely want to visit Prague and Vienna. Would you like to come with us? Write soon, Ruby`,statements:[{text:`Ruby's last exam was maths.`,answer:!0},{text:`Ruby has already received her exam results.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ruby is going to work in a shop in July.`,answer:!1},{text:`Ruby and Katie want to visit Vienna.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-099`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'It is not one single wall', 'built over about two thousand years', 'built to protect China from attacks' and 'other parts have fallen down'.`,passage:`The Great Wall of China is one of the most famous buildings in the world. It is not one single wall, but many walls which were built over about two thousand years. The total length of all the sections is more than twenty thousand kilometres. The walls were built to protect China from attacks from the north. Millions of workers helped to build them, and many of them died during the work. Today, some parts of the wall are in good condition and are visited by thousands of tourists every day, while other parts have fallen down.`,statements:[{text:`The Great Wall is one single wall.`,answer:!1},{text:`The wall was built in a few years.`,answer:!1},{text:`The wall was built to protect China.`,answer:!0},{text:`All parts of the wall are in good condition today.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-100`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says 'He used to be an accountant', 'sold them at local markets', 'he has employed two people to help him' and 'he earns less than before'.`,passage:`Owen started his own online business selling handmade wooden toys two years ago. He used to be an accountant, but he wasn't happy sitting at a desk all day. He had always enjoyed working with wood, so he decided to turn his hobby into a job. At first he made only a few toys a week and sold them at local markets. Then he created a website and started selling all over the country. Now he can't make the toys fast enough, so he has employed two people to help him. He says he earns less than before but he is much happier.`,statements:[{text:`Owen used to work as an accountant.`,answer:!0},{text:`Owen first sold his toys at markets.`,answer:!0},{text:`Owen makes all the toys by himself.`,answer:!1},{text:`Owen earns less money than in his old job.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-101`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "do not exercise regularly", "lack of time and tiredness", "even short sessions ... can improve".`,passage:`A survey has found that more than half of adults in the country do not exercise regularly. The most common excuses are lack of time and tiredness after work. Health experts recommend at least a hundred and fifty minutes of moderate activity every week, such as brisk walking or swimming. They point out that even short sessions of ten minutes, repeated throughout the day, can improve fitness and mood.`,statements:[{text:`Most adults exercise regularly.`,answer:!1},{text:`Lack of time is a common excuse.`,answer:!0},{text:`Short exercise sessions are useless.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-102`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "in spring it is calm", "fresh grilled sardines", "lower outside the main season".`,passage:`The beach at Praia da Rocha in Portugal is famous for its golden cliffs. In summer it is crowded, but in spring it is calm and the water is clean. Local restaurants serve fresh grilled sardines, and the prices are lower outside the main season. A short walk along the cliffs leads to a series of hidden coves. Many visitors say that spring is the best time to go.`,statements:[{text:`The beach is crowded in spring.`,answer:!1},{text:`Restaurants offer fresh sardines.`,answer:!0},{text:`Prices are lower outside the main season.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-103`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "popular again", "hundreds of games", "takes an hour to read the rules".`,passage:`Over the last few years, board games have become popular again. Many cafés now offer hundreds of games, and groups of friends spend whole evenings around a table instead of looking at their phones. The owners say that customers like the chance to talk and laugh in person. Some games are so complicated that it takes an hour to read the rules, but players say that this is part of the fun.`,statements:[{text:`Board games are becoming less popular.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some cafés offer many games.`,answer:!0},{text:`Reading the rules is always quick.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-104`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "her uncle's garage", "in the evenings she attended a course", "hopes to open her own garage one day".`,passage:`After finishing school, Marta started working in her uncle's garage. She cleaned tools and watched the mechanics, and in the evenings she attended a course in car repair. Two years later she passed her exams and became one of the few women mechanics in the town. Some customers were surprised to see her, but now they ask for her by name. She hopes to open her own garage one day.`,statements:[{text:`Marta worked in her uncle's garage.`,answer:!0},{text:`She studied at night.`,answer:!0},{text:`She already owns a garage.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-105`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "does not know anybody", "once a month", "made it easy to talk to people".`,passage:`Sam has just moved to a new town and does not know anybody. To make friends, he joined a running club and a book group. At the beginning he felt shy, but the members were friendly. Now he runs with the club twice a week and meets the book group once a month. He says that having a regular activity made it easy to talk to people.`,statements:[{text:`Sam knew many people in the new town.`,answer:!1},{text:`He meets the book group once a month.`,answer:!0},{text:`Regular activities helped him make friends.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-106`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "shy student", "join the debating club", "skills she now uses in her job".`,passage:`Ten years ago, Nora was a shy student who hated speaking in public. A teacher advised her to join the debating club. At first she only listened, but gradually she began to speak. Last year Nora won a national debating competition. She says that the club taught her to organise her ideas and to remain calm, skills she now uses in her job as a lawyer.`,statements:[{text:`Nora was a confident speaker as a student.`,answer:!1},{text:`She joined a debating club.`,answer:!0},{text:`Her skills help her in her job.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-107`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "For two days we had no water", "on the third day", "wrapped them".`,passage:`Because of the cold weather, our pipes froze last winter. For two days we had no water, and we had to melt snow to wash. A plumber finally arrived on the third day and repaired the pipe. He explained that we should have wrapped them with material to protect them from the cold. This year we have already done so, and my father has also bought a spare heater in case of another emergency.`,statements:[{text:`The family had no water for two days.`,answer:!0},{text:`The plumber arrived on the first day.`,answer:!1},{text:`The family has taken precautions.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-108`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "does not have a swimming pool", "a former chef", "praise the friendly staff".`,passage:`The Hotel Aurora is a small family-run hotel on the coast. All the rooms have sea views, and breakfast is served on a terrace. The owner, a former chef, prepares fish dishes in the evening. The hotel does not have a swimming pool, but guests can use the nearby beach. Reviews on the internet praise the friendly staff and the calm atmosphere.`,statements:[{text:`The hotel has a swimming pool.`,answer:!1},{text:`The owner used to be a chef.`,answer:!0},{text:`Reviews mention friendly staff.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-109`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "lasts only four hours", "double the chance of survival", "free for students".`,passage:`The Red Cross trains volunteers to give first aid. A short course teaches how to help someone who is choking, how to stop bleeding and how to start the heart again with massage. Over the last ten years, more than two million people have attended the course. Doctors say that quick help from a bystander can double the chance of survival. The course lasts only four hours and is free for students.`,statements:[{text:`The first aid course is long.`,answer:!1},{text:`Immediate help can increase the chance of survival.`,answer:!0},{text:`Students pay for the course.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-110`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "arrive ten minutes early", "show interest by asking questions", "honest about their weaknesses".`,passage:`The job interview is often the most stressful part of looking for work. Experts advise candidates to research the company, to practise answers to typical questions and to arrive ten minutes early. During the interview it is important to show interest by asking questions. Many employers say that they remember candidates who are honest about their weaknesses and show that they are willing to learn.`,statements:[{text:`Experts recommend arriving late.`,answer:!1},{text:`Asking questions shows interest.`,answer:!0},{text:`Employers like honesty about weaknesses.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-111`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Within hours", "Schools were turned into shelters", "promised to rebuild".`,passage:`After the earthquake, thousands of people lost their homes. Within hours, volunteers from nearby towns arrived with food, blankets and medicine. Schools were turned into shelters, and local restaurants cooked meals for free. The government promised to rebuild the damaged houses within two years. A young engineer who lost his own home said that the kindness of strangers had given him the strength to continue.`,statements:[{text:`Volunteers arrived after several weeks.`,answer:!1},{text:`Schools were used as shelters.`,answer:!0},{text:`The government promised to rebuild the houses.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-112`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Every Tuesday morning", "volunteering", "ask their parents to read the same stories".`,passage:`Mrs Taylor has been volunteering at the local library for twelve years. Every Tuesday morning she reads stories to young children. She chooses books with colourful pictures and uses different voices for the characters. The children listen carefully, and many of them go home and ask their parents to read the same stories. Mrs Taylor says that seeing a child fall in love with books is the best reward.`,statements:[{text:`Mrs Taylor works at the library on Tuesdays.`,answer:!0},{text:`She is paid for her work.`,answer:!1},{text:`Children ask their parents to read the same stories.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-113`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "connects shops with people", "at a low price", "all major cities".`,passage:`In some countries, unwanted food is a big problem. Supermarkets throw away tonnes of bread and vegetables that are still good to eat. A young entrepreneur started a mobile app that connects shops with people who want to collect the surplus food at a low price. Within a year, the app had saved the equivalent of fifty thousand meals. The founder hopes to make it available in all major cities by the end of next year.`,statements:[{text:`The app helps to reduce food waste.`,answer:!0},{text:`The food is given away to the shops.`,answer:!1},{text:`The founder wants to expand to more cities.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-114`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "travelled alone", "cheap bed and breakfasts", "will definitely do it again".`,passage:`Last summer Helen travelled alone to Scotland for the first time. She hired a small car and drove along the west coast, stopping wherever she found a beautiful view. She slept in cheap bed and breakfasts, where the owners often gave her tips about places that tourists seldom visit. One evening she met a group of walkers who invited her to join them the next day. Helen says that travelling alone made her more independent and that she will definitely do it again.`,statements:[{text:`Helen travelled with friends.`,answer:!1},{text:`She stayed in bed and breakfasts.`,answer:!0},{text:`She would like to travel alone again.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-115`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "teaching Spanish", "The classes are free", "found jobs thanks to their improved language skills".`,passage:`When Mr Lopez retired, he did not want to sit at home. He started teaching Spanish to immigrants at the community centre. The classes are free, and about thirty people attend each week. Mr Lopez says that his students' enthusiasm gives him energy. Some of them have found jobs thanks to their improved language skills, and they come back to thank him.`,statements:[{text:`Mr Lopez teaches English.`,answer:!1},{text:`The classes cost money.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some students found jobs after attending.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-116`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "only if the teacher asks", "more focused", "can contact their children through the school office".`,passage:`The headteacher of our school has introduced a new policy: pupils may use their phones during lessons only if the teacher asks them to. Before, many students kept their phones under the desk and checked messages. Teachers say that the lessons are now more focused. A few students complain, but others admit that they were distracted before. Parents have been informed and can contact their children through the school office.`,statements:[{text:`Phones are always banned in the classroom.`,answer:!1},{text:`Teachers say lessons are more focused.`,answer:!0},{text:`Parents cannot reach their children.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-117`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "on the second attempt", "a very patient man", "forgot to check my mirror".`,passage:`Learning to drive was harder than I expected. In the first lesson I stalled the car five times, and my instructor, a very patient man called Mr Evans, laughed and told me not to worry. After ten lessons I could drive on quiet roads, but busy junctions still made me nervous. I passed my test on the second attempt. The first time I failed because I forgot to check my mirror before turning, which seems silly now.`,statements:[{text:`The writer passed the driving test on the first attempt.`,answer:!1},{text:`Mr Evans was a patient instructor.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer failed once because of forgetting something.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-118`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "painted them herself", "Instead of buying new furniture", "could not believe the change".`,passage:`Karen decided to redecorate her living room on a small budget. She chose a pale green colour for the walls and painted them herself over a weekend. Instead of buying new furniture, she covered the old sofa with a bright blanket and added cushions from a charity shop. The most expensive item was a lamp, which cost twenty euros. Her friends could not believe the change and asked her for advice.`,statements:[{text:`Karen hired professionals to paint the room.`,answer:!1},{text:`She bought new furniture.`,answer:!1},{text:`Her friends were impressed.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-119`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "talk to current students", "change quickly", "problem solving and communication".`,passage:`Choosing a university course is a big decision. Many students pick subjects that sound impressive but later discover that they do not enjoy them. Career advisers suggest that young people visit open days, talk to current students and think about what they like doing in their free time. They also warn that job markets change quickly, so skills such as problem solving and communication are often more valuable than a specific degree.`,statements:[{text:`Career advisers recommend talking to current students.`,answer:!0},{text:`Job markets never change.`,answer:!1},{text:`General skills can be more valuable than a specific degree.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-120`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "software company", "instead of blaming", "lowest turnover".`,passage:`Mia manages a team of ten people in a software company. She says that the key to good management is listening. She meets each team member once a week to ask about problems and ideas. When someone makes a mistake, she tries to understand what happened instead of blaming. Her team has the lowest turnover in the company, and she has been voted "manager of the year" twice.`,statements:[{text:`Mia works in a software company.`,answer:!0},{text:`She blames people when they make mistakes.`,answer:!1},{text:`Her team has a low turnover.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-121`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "every Saturday morning", "mostly plastic bottles", "has promised to give them".`,passage:`A group of volunteers meets every Saturday morning to clean the beach near our town. They bring gloves, bags and a small scale to weigh the rubbish. Last month they collected more than two hundred kilos, mostly plastic bottles and old fishing nets. The volunteers are of all ages, from schoolchildren to retired teachers. After the cleaning, they have a picnic together and plan the following week's activities. The mayor has promised to give them a small boat to reach more remote bays.`,statements:[{text:`The volunteers work on the beach once a month.`,answer:!1},{text:`Most of the rubbish was plastic.`,answer:!0},{text:`The mayor has already given them a boat.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-122`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "a boy of twelve knocked at my door", "not even the money", "refused it at first".`,passage:`A week ago, I lost my wallet in the street. I was sure I would never see it again. Two days later, a boy of twelve knocked at my door. He had found the wallet and used the address on my ID card to return it. Nothing was missing, not even the money. I gave him a reward, but he refused it at first and only accepted after I insisted.`,statements:[{text:`The writer found the wallet alone.`,answer:!1},{text:`Nothing was missing from the wallet.`,answer:!0},{text:`The boy accepted the reward immediately.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-123`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "hundreds of years", "fell by ninety per cent", "used for environmental projects".`,passage:`Plastic bags take hundreds of years to break down, and many end up in the sea where animals eat them by mistake. Several countries have therefore introduced a small charge for each bag in supermarkets. In Ireland, the number of bags used fell by ninety per cent after the charge started. People now bring their own bags, and the money collected is used for environmental projects. Critics say that the charge hurts poorer families, but most people support the idea.`,statements:[{text:`Plastic bags disappear quickly in nature.`,answer:!1},{text:`In Ireland the charge reduced the number of bags used.`,answer:!0},{text:`The money from the charge is kept by the supermarkets.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-124`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "found that the centre brought more visitors", "helped the small shops", "miss the quiet atmosphere".`,passage:`When the new shopping centre opened, local shop owners feared that they would lose customers. Instead, many of them found that the centre brought more visitors to the area. The council helped the small shops with advertising and lower rents. Today, the old market street has a lively mix of traditional stores and new cafés. Some residents, however, miss the quiet atmosphere the street had before.`,statements:[{text:`The local shops lost all their customers.`,answer:!1},{text:`The council supported the small shops.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some residents prefer the street as it was.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-125`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "without needing a medical certificate", "more productive", "fallen by a fifth".`,passage:`Many companies are now offering "mental health days" to their employees. These are days off that workers can take when they feel too stressed to work, without needing a medical certificate. Supporters say that rested employees are more productive and less likely to become seriously ill. Critics worry that some people might abuse the system. Early results from one firm show that sick leave has fallen by a fifth since the policy began.`,statements:[{text:`Employees need a doctor's note for a mental health day.`,answer:!1},{text:`Supporters think rested workers are more productive.`,answer:!0},{text:`Sick leave has increased.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-126`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "cheaper than staying in a hotel", "leaving no rubbish behind", "how cold it gets at night".`,passage:`Camping is cheaper than staying in a hotel and gives you a closer contact with nature. However, it also requires planning. You must choose a flat place for the tent, bring enough water, and check the weather forecast. Experienced campers advise leaving no rubbish behind and avoiding lighting fires in dry areas. Beginners are often surprised by how cold it gets at night, even in summer.`,statements:[{text:`Camping is more expensive than hotels.`,answer:!1},{text:`Campers should not leave rubbish.`,answer:!0},{text:`Nights can be cold in summer.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-127`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "are sometimes criticised", "colours that birds can see", "receive a share of the profits".`,passage:`Wind farms produce clean electricity but they are sometimes criticised. Some people say that the tall turbines spoil the view and make a noise. Birds can also be hurt if the turbines are built in the wrong place. Engineers are now designing turbines that turn more slowly and are painted in colours that birds can see more easily. Many communities accept wind farms when they receive a share of the profits.`,statements:[{text:`Wind farms never receive criticism.`,answer:!1},{text:`Engineers are trying to make turbines safer for birds.`,answer:!0},{text:`Communities cannot benefit from wind farms.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-128`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "first weekend of September", "On Saturday there is a parade", "book rooms months in advance".`,passage:`The village festival takes place on the first weekend of September. On Saturday there is a parade with brass bands and decorated carts. The streets are filled with stalls selling cheese, honey and handmade toys. In the evening, everyone eats together in the main square, and there is dancing until midnight. Visitors from nearby towns come every year and many book rooms months in advance.`,statements:[{text:`The festival is in September.`,answer:!0},{text:`The parade takes place on Sunday.`,answer:!1},{text:`Visitors often book accommodation early.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-129`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "keeps chickens", "share them with neighbours", "a fox that sometimes visits at night".`,passage:`Emily's family keeps chickens in the garden. Every morning the children collect the eggs and give them fresh water. In the summer the family has more eggs than they can eat, so they share them with neighbours. Emily says the chickens are friendly and that each one has a name. The only problem is a fox that sometimes visits at night, so the father has built a stronger fence.`,statements:[{text:`The family keeps chickens.`,answer:!0},{text:`They sell eggs in a shop.`,answer:!1},{text:`A fox has caused problems.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-130`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "walk or cycle to work", "receive a tax reduction", "increased by fifteen per cent".`,passage:`The government has launched a campaign to encourage people to walk or cycle to work. Advertisements on buses show smiling workers arriving at the office on their bikes. Companies that offer showers and safe places to park bicycles receive a tax reduction. After one year, the number of people cycling to work has increased by fifteen per cent. Experts say that this is good for the environment and also reduces illness among workers.`,statements:[{text:`The campaign wants people to use cars more.`,answer:!1},{text:`Companies with showers and bike parking receive a benefit.`,answer:!0},{text:`The number of cyclists decreased.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-131`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "not always easy", "colleagues were friendly", "thinking of applying for permanent residence".`,passage:`Working abroad can be a great experience, but it is not always easy. Adrian moved to Canada for a job in engineering. He found that colleagues were friendly, but the winters were harsh and he missed his family. Learning the local way of doing business took time, and he made several mistakes in the beginning. After two years, he feels at home and is thinking of applying for permanent residence.`,statements:[{text:`Adrian found everything simple.`,answer:!1},{text:`Adrian's colleagues were friendly.`,answer:!0},{text:`He may stay in Canada permanently.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-132`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "for ten years", "they forget about the evenings and weekends", "thinking about taking a year off to travel".`,passage:`I have been working as a primary school teacher for ten years. People often say I am lucky because I have long holidays, but they forget about the evenings and weekends I spend preparing lessons and marking homework. The best part of the job is seeing a child suddenly understand something. The worst part is the paperwork. I am thinking about taking a year off to travel, but I know I would miss my pupils too much.`,statements:[{text:`The writer has been teaching for ten years.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer thinks the job is easy because of the holidays.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer wants to take a year to travel.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-133`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "translate texts, write simple reports", "Some experts fear ... while others believe", "keep learning new skills".`,passage:`Artificial intelligence is changing many jobs. Programs can already translate texts, write simple reports and help doctors to read scans. Some experts fear that millions of workers will lose their jobs, while others believe that new kinds of work will appear, as happened during earlier industrial revolutions. Everyone agrees that people will have to keep learning new skills throughout their careers.`,statements:[{text:`AI can already perform some tasks.`,answer:!0},{text:`All experts agree that millions will become unemployed.`,answer:!1},{text:`People will need to keep learning.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-134`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "grown rapidly", "deliver goods on bicycles", "buying fewer things is the best solution".`,passage:`Online shopping has grown rapidly in the last decade. It is convenient and sometimes cheaper, but it also creates more packaging waste and delivery traffic. Some companies are now offering to deliver goods on bicycles or in reusable boxes. Customers can also choose a slower delivery option that reduces the number of journeys. Environmental groups welcome these changes but say that buying fewer things is the best solution.`,statements:[{text:`Online shopping has declined.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some delivery companies use bicycles.`,answer:!0},{text:`Environmental groups think buying less is best.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-135`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "every Friday", "continued ever since", "have to sit on the stairs".`,passage:`Mr and Mrs Brown have a tradition: every Friday they have fish and chips for dinner and play cards afterwards. They started this when their children were small and have continued ever since. Now the children have moved out, but they often come back on Fridays with their own families. Mrs Brown says the table is sometimes so crowded that people have to sit on the stairs, but nobody minds.`,statements:[{text:`The Browns eat fish and chips on Fridays.`,answer:!0},{text:`The tradition ended when the children left.`,answer:!1},{text:`Family members sometimes sit on the stairs.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-136`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "most of them get less than seven", "stay up late to use their phones", "turning off all screens an hour before bedtime".`,passage:`Many young people today say that they feel stressed. Research shows that a lack of sleep is one of the main causes. Teenagers need about nine hours of sleep a night, but most of them get less than seven because they stay up late to use their phones. Doctors advise turning off all screens an hour before bedtime and doing something relaxing, such as reading or listening to quiet music. Students who follow this advice often report that they concentrate better at school.`,statements:[{text:`Teenagers usually get nine hours of sleep.`,answer:!1},{text:`Screens can make it harder to sleep.`,answer:!0},{text:`Doctors recommend using the phone just before bed.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-137`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "essential tools in many jobs", "reduce concentration", "only at fixed times".`,passage:`Smartphones have become essential tools in many jobs. Delivery drivers use them to find addresses, doctors check patient information, and farmers receive weather alerts. However, constant notifications can reduce concentration. Productivity experts recommend turning off alerts that are not urgent and checking messages only at fixed times. Workers who do so report that they finish tasks faster and feel less stressed.`,statements:[{text:`Smartphones are used only for entertainment.`,answer:!1},{text:`Notifications can reduce concentration.`,answer:!0},{text:`Experts suggest checking messages at fixed times.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-138`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "a trainee in a law firm", "felt lost", "learning more in a week than at university in a month".`,passage:`Jenny has just started her first job as a trainee in a law firm. On the first day she was given a desk, a computer and a long list of files to read. She felt lost until a colleague showed her around and explained the abbreviations. Now, after a month, she understands most of what is going on. She works long hours, but she says that she is learning more in a week than at university in a month.`,statements:[{text:`Jenny works in a law firm.`,answer:!0},{text:`She understood everything on day one.`,answer:!1},{text:`She thinks she learns a lot.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-139`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "never grown vegetables before", "asked an elderly neighbour", "more lettuce and beans than they can eat".`,passage:`After years of living in a flat, Mark and Lisa bought a small house with a garden. They had never grown vegetables before and made many mistakes. Their first tomatoes were eaten by slugs, and the carrots never grew. They asked an elderly neighbour for advice, and he gave them tips and some seeds. This year they have more lettuce and beans than they can eat.`,statements:[{text:`Mark and Lisa had experience in gardening.`,answer:!1},{text:`A neighbour helped them.`,answer:!0},{text:`This year the garden is successful.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-140`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Instead of a party in a restaurant", "where she had spent her childhood", "garden of our grandparents' house".`,passage:`We celebrated my sister's twenty-first birthday in an unusual way. Instead of a party in a restaurant, we organised a treasure hunt through the town. Her friends had to follow clues that led to different places where she had spent her childhood: her old school, the ice-cream shop and the park where she learned to ride a bike. At the end, they found a cake and a present hidden in the garden of our grandparents' house. She said it was the best birthday she had ever had.`,statements:[{text:`The party took place in a restaurant.`,answer:!1},{text:`The clues led to places connected with her childhood.`,answer:!0},{text:`The present was found at the grandparents' house.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-141`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "the whole family cried", "nothing like our old dog", "from the animal shelter".`,passage:`It's difficult to say goodbye to a pet. When our old dog died last year, the whole family cried. We buried him in the garden under his favourite tree and planted flowers on the spot. For weeks the house felt empty. Recently we adopted a puppy from the animal shelter. He is nothing like our old dog, which is exactly why we love him: he makes us laugh and has given us something to look forward to.`,statements:[{text:`The family cried when the dog died.`,answer:!0},{text:`The new puppy is exactly like the old dog.`,answer:!1},{text:`The family adopted the puppy from a shelter.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-142`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "on certain days", "Public transport was free", "Some shop owners complained".`,passage:`Air pollution is a serious problem in many big cities. In Madrid, for example, cars were banned from the city centre on certain days last winter to reduce the smoke. Public transport was free on those days, and bicycles were available at no cost. The result was a clear improvement in the quality of the air. Some shop owners complained that fewer customers came, but others said the streets felt calmer and more pleasant to walk in.`,statements:[{text:`Cars were banned from the centre on all days.`,answer:!1},{text:`Public transport was free on the days with the ban.`,answer:!0},{text:`Every shop owner supported the measure.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-143`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "connect the airport with the city centre", "four years", "better spent on schools and hospitals".`,passage:`The government wants to reduce the number of cars on the road by building a new underground line. The line will connect the airport with the city centre in twenty minutes. Construction will take four years and will cost two billion euros. Opponents say that the money would be better spent on schools and hospitals. Supporters reply that fewer cars will mean cleaner air and fewer traffic jams.`,statements:[{text:`The new line will connect the airport with the centre.`,answer:!0},{text:`Construction will take only one year.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people think the money should be used elsewhere.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-144`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "no shop, no bar", "left them bread, eggs and cheese", "the most relaxing holiday".`,passage:`Anna and Pablo wanted a quiet holiday, so they chose a small village in the mountains. There was no shop, no bar and almost no mobile signal. The owner of their cottage left them bread, eggs and cheese on the first day. During the week they walked, read and cooked simple meals. On the last night, they sat outside to look at the stars. They agreed it was the most relaxing holiday of their lives.`,statements:[{text:`The village had many shops.`,answer:!1},{text:`The owner left food for them.`,answer:!0},{text:`They felt relaxed.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-145`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "hated getting up early", "go running before work", "surprised that I have so much energy".`,passage:`When I was a child I hated getting up early. Now I get up at five thirty every morning and go running before work. I discovered that the streets are empty and quiet, and I can think clearly. After the run I have a shower and a big breakfast. My colleagues are surprised that I have so much energy at nine o'clock. I would never have imagined that I could become a morning person.`,statements:[{text:`The writer always liked getting up early.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer runs in the morning.`,answer:!0},{text:`Colleagues are surprised by the writer's energy.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-146`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "two years instead of three", "enter the labour market sooner", "best for highly motivated people".`,passage:`Some universities now offer degrees that can be completed in two years instead of three by studying during the summer. Students save money on accommodation and enter the labour market sooner. However, the programme is intense, and there is less time for sport or part-time work. A few students have left the course because of stress. Professors suggest that the programme is best for highly motivated people.`,statements:[{text:`The accelerated degree takes four years.`,answer:!1},{text:`Students enter work earlier.`,answer:!0},{text:`The course is suitable for everyone.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-147`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "arrived two hours late", "lift it through the window", "very happy in our new home".`,passage:`Moving house is stressful, as I discovered last month. We packed our things into more than eighty boxes, and the removal van arrived two hours late. When we got to the new flat, we realised that the sofa did not fit through the door, so the removal men had to lift it through the window. Despite all the problems, we are very happy in our new home, which has a larger kitchen and a balcony with a view of the park.`,statements:[{text:`The removal van arrived on time.`,answer:!1},{text:`The sofa was lifted through the window.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer regrets moving.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-148`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "the weather suddenly changed", "brought extra food and warm clothes", "always to check the forecast".`,passage:`Rosa and her family were walking in the mountains when the weather suddenly changed. Dark clouds appeared, and it began to rain heavily. They found a small shelter and waited for two hours. Rosa's father, an experienced walker, had brought extra food and warm clothes, so they were comfortable. When the rain stopped, they walked back down in the sunshine. Rosa says she has learned always to check the forecast.`,statements:[{text:`The family was caught in bad weather.`,answer:!0},{text:`They had no extra food.`,answer:!1},{text:`Rosa now checks the weather forecast.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-149`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "without speaking to each other", "gave the dog some water", "both loved fishing".`,passage:`Chris and Sam were neighbours for years without speaking to each other. One day Chris's dog escaped and ran into Sam's garden. Sam, who loves animals, gave the dog some water and called Chris. They started talking, discovered that they both loved fishing and now go to the lake every Saturday. Chris says that the dog, whom he now calls "the matchmaker", introduced him to his best friend.`,statements:[{text:`The neighbours were friends for years.`,answer:!1},{text:`Sam helped the dog.`,answer:!0},{text:`They share a hobby.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-150`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "three hours late", "offered us a drink", "one of the friendliest cities".`,passage:`We booked a cheap flight to Lisbon, but the trip started badly. The plane was three hours late, and when we arrived at the hotel, our room had not been prepared. The receptionist apologised and offered us a drink while we waited. The next morning the sun was shining, the breakfast was excellent, and by the end of the day we had forgotten the problems. Lisbon turned out to be one of the friendliest cities we have ever visited.`,statements:[{text:`The flight was on time.`,answer:!1},{text:`The hotel offered a drink.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writers enjoyed Lisbon.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-151`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Some teachers say ... while others argue", "quality of homework matters more", "very little homework".`,passage:`There has been a lot of discussion about homework. Some teachers say that it helps pupils to practise what they learned, while others argue that children need free time to play and relax. A school in Finland, where pupils get very little homework, regularly achieves excellent results. Researchers suggest that the quality of homework matters more than quantity: short, meaningful tasks are better than long, repetitive ones.`,statements:[{text:`All teachers agree about homework.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some research says quality is more important than quantity.`,answer:!0},{text:`Finnish pupils get a lot of homework.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-152`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "found the traffic exhausting", "read or listen to podcasts", "The ticket is expensive".`,passage:`Sandra got a new job in another city, which meant a long journey each morning. She tried driving but found the traffic exhausting. Then she started taking the train and discovered that she could read or listen to podcasts during the trip. The ticket is expensive, but she says the time is worth it. After a year, she has finished more than thirty books.`,statements:[{text:`Sandra prefers driving to work.`,answer:!1},{text:`She uses the train journey to read.`,answer:!0},{text:`The train ticket is cheap.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-153`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "stayed with a family", "difficult to understand the local accent", "coming to Italy next month".`,passage:`Marco has just come back from a school exchange in Ireland. He stayed with a family who had two dogs and a farm. Every morning he helped to feed the animals before going to school. At first, he found it difficult to understand the local accent, but after a week it became easier. His host brother is coming to Italy next month, and Marco is planning to take him to the mountains.`,statements:[{text:`Marco stayed in a hotel.`,answer:!1},{text:`He had trouble with the accent at first.`,answer:!0},{text:`The host brother will visit Italy.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-154`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "ninety minutes", "free Wi-Fi", "decreased by almost ten per cent".`,passage:`The new railway line between the two cities has reduced the journey time from four hours to ninety minutes. Passengers can work on the train thanks to free Wi-Fi, and a café car serves breakfast. Ticket prices are slightly higher than for the old line, but most travellers think the speed is worth it. Since the line opened, the number of cars on the motorway has decreased by almost ten per cent.`,statements:[{text:`The journey now takes four hours.`,answer:!1},{text:`The train has Wi-Fi.`,answer:!0},{text:`Motorway traffic has reduced.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-155`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "found it hard", "voluntary work in a charity shop", "offered her a paid position".`,passage:`After graduating, Hannah found it hard to get a job. She sent more than a hundred applications and had only three interviews. She decided to do voluntary work in a charity shop to gain experience. After four months the manager offered her a paid position. Hannah says that the experience taught her patience and that applying for jobs is a skill that improves with practice.`,statements:[{text:`Hannah found a job quickly.`,answer:!1},{text:`She worked as a volunteer.`,answer:!0},{text:`The manager offered her a paid job.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-156`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "snacks, toys and a change of clothes", "play areas", "copy their parents' mood".`,passage:`Travelling with young children requires careful planning. Parents advise packing snacks, toys and a change of clothes in the hand luggage. It also helps to choose flights at the time when the children normally sleep. Many airports now have play areas to keep children busy during long waits. A calm, patient attitude is essential, because children often copy their parents' mood.`,statements:[{text:`Parents should pack toys and snacks.`,answer:!0},{text:`Airports never have play areas.`,answer:!1},{text:`Children copy their parents' mood.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-157`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "only six seconds", "spelling mistakes are a quick way to be rejected", "keeping the CV to one page".`,passage:`Writing a good CV is a skill. Recruiters spend, on average, only six seconds looking at each one at first. They look for clear headings, recent experience and relevant skills. Long paragraphs and spelling mistakes are a quick way to be rejected. Career advisers recommend keeping the CV to one page and adapting it for each job.`,statements:[{text:`Recruiters read each CV carefully for several minutes.`,answer:!1},{text:`Spelling mistakes can lead to rejection.`,answer:!0},{text:`Advisers suggest a one-page CV.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-158`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "arrived at the station just as it was leaving", "the road was closed", "a taxi driver offered to take him".`,passage:`Tom was supposed to take the train to his friend's wedding, but he arrived at the station just as it was leaving. He tried to catch a bus, but the road was closed because of an accident. In the end, a taxi driver offered to take him for a fixed price, and he arrived with only ten minutes to spare. Tom says he has learned his lesson and will leave much earlier next time.`,statements:[{text:`Tom missed the train.`,answer:!0},{text:`The road was open.`,answer:!1},{text:`He arrived at the wedding by taxi.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-159`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "for older people", "many of them teenagers", "a waiting list".`,passage:`The town library has started offering free courses in basic computer skills for older people. They learn how to send emails, use video calls and look for information online. Volunteers, many of them teenagers, help the participants. The classes are popular, and there is a waiting list. A seventy-year-old participant says that she can now see her grandchildren on the screen every week.`,statements:[{text:`The courses are for young people only.`,answer:!1},{text:`Teenagers help in the courses.`,answer:!0},{text:`There is a waiting list.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-160`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "provided they are present during the core hours", "pick them up from school", "Not all departments can use the system".`,passage:`The company where Peter works introduced a new system called "flexible hours". Employees can choose when they start and finish, provided they are present during the core hours from ten to three. Peter, who has two small children, now starts at seven so that he can pick them up from school. His manager says that productivity has not fallen, and staff turnover has decreased. Not all departments can use the system, however, because the reception desk must always be staffed.`,statements:[{text:`Employees may start and finish when they like without any rules.`,answer:!1},{text:`Peter uses the system to look after his children.`,answer:!0},{text:`All departments use the system.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-161`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "borrow a person for thirty minutes", "The service is free", "break down prejudice".`,passage:`The city library has introduced a service called "Human Library". Instead of books, visitors can borrow a person for thirty minutes and listen to their story. The "books" include a refugee, a former prisoner and a woman who lived in the Arctic. The aim is to break down prejudice by letting people talk to someone whose life is very different from their own. The service is free, and booking is necessary because the most popular stories are always reserved weeks in advance.`,statements:[{text:`Visitors can borrow people for half an hour.`,answer:!0},{text:`The service costs five euros.`,answer:!1},{text:`The aim is to reduce prejudice.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-162`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "adding fifteen minutes of exercise to every lesson", "calmer", "test results had improved".`,passage:`Many experts believe that the number of obese children is rising because they spend too much time sitting down. They watch television, play computer games and travel everywhere by car. A school in Leeds decided to change this by adding fifteen minutes of exercise to every lesson. Pupils jump, stretch and run on the spot between tasks. After one term, teachers noticed that pupils were calmer and that their test results had improved.`,statements:[{text:`The school added exercise to lessons.`,answer:!0},{text:`Pupils felt more tired after the change.`,answer:!1},{text:`Test results got better.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-163`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "worried", "further inland", "After a year of protest".`,passage:`Residents of a small coastal village were worried when a large company wanted to build a hotel on the beach. They organised meetings, wrote to newspapers and collected five thousand signatures. After a year of protest, the company decided to build the hotel further inland, away from the nesting area of sea turtles. The villagers celebrated with a party on the beach.`,statements:[{text:`The villagers accepted the hotel immediately.`,answer:!1},{text:`The company changed the location of the hotel.`,answer:!0},{text:`The protest lasted about a year.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-164`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "falling over", "a patient young man", "my legs hurt so much".`,passage:`The first time I went skiing, I spent most of the day falling over. My instructor, a patient young man, taught me how to turn and stop. By the afternoon I could go down a gentle slope without falling. I was exhausted but happy. The next day my legs hurt so much that I could hardly walk, but I wanted to try again. I would recommend skiing to anyone who isn't afraid of looking silly.`,statements:[{text:`The writer was good at skiing from the start.`,answer:!1},{text:`The instructor was patient.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer's legs hurt the next day.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-165`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "practical skills", "half of their time working in companies", "open two more next year".`,passage:`A new vocational school has opened in our region. Students learn practical skills such as plumbing, electrical work and cooking, and spend half of their time working in companies. Employers say that graduates are well prepared and find jobs quickly. The school has a waiting list, and the government plans to open two more next year. Parents who once wanted their children to go to university are now looking at this option too.`,statements:[{text:`The school teaches practical skills.`,answer:!0},{text:`Students never work in companies.`,answer:!1},{text:`The government plans more schools of this kind.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-166`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "reduce the risk of heart disease", "do not need special equipment", "walking meetings".`,passage:`Doctors say that a daily walk of thirty minutes can reduce the risk of heart disease. It does not cost anything, and you do not need special equipment. Many people find it easier to walk if they have a friend or a dog. Some companies even organise walking meetings where employees discuss ideas outdoors. Participants say that they feel more creative and less tired than in a normal meeting in the office.`,statements:[{text:`A daily walk can protect the heart.`,answer:!0},{text:`You need expensive equipment to walk.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some companies hold meetings while walking.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-167`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "feeling of security", "doesn't matter what you do", "repeat them with their own families".`,passage:`Regular family traditions give children a feeling of security. In many homes, Sunday is the day for a big breakfast, a walk or a game together. Experts say that it doesn't matter what you do, as long as you do it regularly. Children remember these moments for the rest of their lives and often repeat them with their own families.`,statements:[{text:`Traditions give children security.`,answer:!0},{text:`Experts say the activity itself is crucial.`,answer:!1},{text:`Children often repeat traditions as adults.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-168`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "dress modestly in temples", "remove your shoes", "learning about local customs".`,passage:`In some countries, tourists are asked to follow special rules. In Thailand, for example, visitors must dress modestly in temples and never touch a person's head. In Japan, it is polite to remove your shoes when you enter a home. Guidebooks recommend learning about local customs before the trip, to avoid giving offence by mistake. Most people are forgiving when visitors try to be respectful.`,statements:[{text:`Dress rules apply in Thai temples.`,answer:!0},{text:`In Japan people keep shoes on indoors.`,answer:!1},{text:`Guidebooks advise learning about customs.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-169`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "cheap and convenient", "can cause health problems", "an occasional burger is not a problem".`,passage:`Fast food is cheap and convenient, but doctors warn that eating it too often can cause health problems. Burgers, chips and sugary drinks contain a lot of fat and salt, and very few vitamins. A study of two thousand teenagers found that those who ate fast food more than three times a week were more likely to be overweight. However, experts say that an occasional burger is not a problem if the rest of your diet is balanced.`,statements:[{text:`Fast food is expensive.`,answer:!1},{text:`Eating fast food often can be bad for your health.`,answer:!0},{text:`Experts say you must never eat a burger.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-170`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "mild climate", "irrigation channels", "steep and winding".`,passage:`The island of Madeira is known as the "garden of the Atlantic" because of its flowers and mild climate. It is popular with walkers, who follow old irrigation channels through forests and mountains. The capital, Funchal, has a lively market where you can taste tropical fruit. Although the island is small, the roads are steep and winding, so driving can be tiring. Many visitors prefer to rent a guide with a car.`,statements:[{text:`Madeira has a cold climate.`,answer:!1},{text:`Walkers follow irrigation channels.`,answer:!0},{text:`Driving on the island can be tiring.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-171`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "argued about everything", "a line on the floor with tape", "getting on much better".`,passage:`Lucy and her brother have to share a bedroom because their flat is small. At first they argued about everything: the light, the noise, the temperature. Then their mother suggested drawing a line on the floor with tape to divide the room. Each child decorated their half in their own style, and they agreed not to cross the line without asking. After a few weeks, they were getting on much better.`,statements:[{text:`The siblings agreed on everything at first.`,answer:!1},{text:`The room was divided with tape.`,answer:!0},{text:`The arrangement improved their relationship.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-172`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "banned cigarettes in all public parks", "Parents welcomed the decision", "Similar rules already exist".`,passage:`The mayor of a small Italian town has banned cigarettes in all public parks. Anyone caught smoking must pay a fine of fifty euros. Parents welcomed the decision because children often find cigarette ends on the ground. Smokers say that the ban is too strict, but the mayor argues that parks should be healthy places for everyone. Similar rules already exist in several other cities in Europe.`,statements:[{text:`Smoking is allowed in the parks.`,answer:!1},{text:`Parents were happy about the ban.`,answer:!0},{text:`Similar rules are completely new in Europe.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-173`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "one of the most visited cities", "Rising sea levels cause floods", "others say that it will not solve".`,passage:`Venice is one of the most visited cities in the world, but it is also in danger. The number of tourists is so high that residents sometimes find it hard to walk through the narrow streets. Rising sea levels cause floods, which damage historic buildings. The city has introduced a small entrance fee for day visitors in the busiest periods. Some people believe that this is a good idea, while others say that it will not solve the main problem.`,statements:[{text:`Venice has very few visitors.`,answer:!1},{text:`Floods damage historic buildings.`,answer:!0},{text:`Everyone thinks the fee is a perfect solution.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-174`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "compare prices in seconds", "starting to offer their own apps", "makes them spend more".`,passage:`Mobile apps have changed the way we shop. Customers can now compare prices in seconds, pay with their phone and have their groceries delivered to the door. Small shops that cannot compete with the big supermarkets are starting to offer their own apps, with discounts for regular customers. Some people worry that online shopping makes them spend more because buying is so easy. Others say it helps them to save time and avoid queues.`,statements:[{text:`Apps make it easy to compare prices.`,answer:!0},{text:`Small shops refuse to use apps.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people think online shopping can lead to spending more.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-175`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Even people who do not smoke can be harmed", "many countries have banned", "never too late to stop".`,passage:`Smoking is one of the main causes of lung disease. Even people who do not smoke can be harmed by breathing the smoke of others. This is why many countries have banned smoking in restaurants and offices. Since the ban started in Ireland, studies have shown that heart attacks have become less frequent. Doctors encourage smokers to try nicotine patches or join support groups, and they say that it is never too late to stop.`,statements:[{text:`Only smokers are harmed by smoke.`,answer:!1},{text:`Smoking bans are in force in some countries.`,answer:!0},{text:`Doctors say it is too late to stop after some years.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-176`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "handwritten letter", "his childhood on a farm", "keep the letter in a box".`,passage:`The best present I ever received was a handwritten letter from my grandfather. He wrote about his childhood on a farm, the games he played and his first day at school. I read it at least ten times. He died two years ago, and I now keep the letter in a box with other memories. I have decided to write a similar letter to my own grandchildren one day.`,statements:[{text:`The writer received a recorded message.`,answer:!1},{text:`The grandfather wrote about his childhood.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer keeps the letter.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-177`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "not salary but relations with colleagues", "less likely to change jobs", "small gestures".`,passage:`A survey of employees found that the most important factor in job satisfaction is not salary but relations with colleagues. People who feel respected by their team are less likely to change jobs. Managers can improve the atmosphere by thanking people for good work, listening to ideas and organising social activities. Even small gestures, such as bringing coffee for the team, can make a difference.`,statements:[{text:`Salary is the most important factor.`,answer:!1},{text:`Respect from colleagues reduces job changes.`,answer:!0},{text:`Small gestures can improve the atmosphere.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-178`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "stop offering televisions", "a board game", "fully booked all summer".`,passage:`A small hotel in the mountains has decided to stop offering televisions in the bedrooms. Instead, guests are given a board game and a book of local walks. The owner explains that she wants people to talk to each other and enjoy the surroundings. At first some guests complained, but most of them now say that they sleep better and feel more relaxed. The hotel has become so popular that it is fully booked all summer.`,statements:[{text:`The hotel has televisions in every room.`,answer:!1},{text:`Guests receive a board game.`,answer:!0},{text:`The hotel is difficult to book in summer.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-179`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "visually impaired", "twenty volunteers", "offered them funding".`,passage:`A group of students designed an app that helps visually impaired people to find their way in cities. The app uses the phone's camera to recognise objects and gives spoken directions. After testing it with twenty volunteers, the students improved the speed and accuracy. A technology company has now offered them funding to develop it further. The students say they never imagined a school project would turn into a business.`,statements:[{text:`The app is for people with a visual problem.`,answer:!0},{text:`Only five volunteers tested it.`,answer:!1},{text:`A company offered funding.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-180`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "cause stress and sleeping problems", "horns are not allowed", "shown on a public map".`,passage:`There is growing concern about noise pollution in cities. Constant traffic, building work and loud music can cause stress and sleeping problems. Some cities have introduced "quiet zones" around hospitals and schools, where horns are not allowed. In Paris, sensors now measure the noise in different districts, and the results are shown on a public map. Residents say they feel their opinions are finally being taken seriously.`,statements:[{text:`Noise can cause stress.`,answer:!0},{text:`Quiet zones allow all kinds of horns.`,answer:!1},{text:`Paris shows noise levels on a map.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-181`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Many teenagers prefer", "phones must be left in another room", "conversation has improved".`,passage:`Mobile phones have changed the way people talk to each other. Many teenagers prefer sending messages to making phone calls, and some say they feel uncomfortable speaking on the phone. Parents often complain that their children look at their screens during meals. Some families have introduced a rule that phones must be left in another room at dinner time. Those families say that conversation has improved and that the whole family now enjoys eating together.`,statements:[{text:`All teenagers hate phone calls.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some families do not allow phones at dinner.`,answer:!0},{text:`The rule has improved conversation in those families.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-182`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "under construction for more than a hundred years", "sold online", "more impressive than the outside".`,passage:`The city of Barcelona is famous for the architecture of Antoni Gaudí. His most famous building, the Sagrada Família, has been under construction for more than a hundred years. Tickets are sold online, and queues can be long in summer. Visitors say that the inside of the church, with its tall columns and coloured light, is more impressive than the outside. The building is expected to be completed in the next few years.`,statements:[{text:`The Sagrada Família was finished long ago.`,answer:!1},{text:`Tickets can be bought online.`,answer:!0},{text:`Visitors admire the inside very much.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-183`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "requires all cyclists to wear a helmet", "have fallen sharply", "cheap helmets to students".`,passage:`A new law in our country requires all cyclists to wear a helmet. Before the law, only about a quarter of cyclists used one. Hospital doctors say that head injuries from bicycle accidents have fallen sharply since then. Some cyclists argue that the law is unnecessary and that they should be free to choose. The government replies that safety is more important than personal preference and has offered cheap helmets to students.`,statements:[{text:`The law obliges cyclists to wear helmets.`,answer:!0},{text:`Head injuries have increased.`,answer:!1},{text:`The government gives free helmets to everybody.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-184`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "save up to three lives", "given a snack and a drink", "more than a thousand new people".`,passage:`Blood donors are always needed in hospitals. A single donation can help to save up to three lives. The process takes about forty minutes, and donors are given a snack and a drink afterwards. People between eighteen and sixty-five who are in good health can give blood every three months. Last year, a local campaign persuaded more than a thousand new people to become regular donors.`,statements:[{text:`A donation can help several people.`,answer:!0},{text:`Donors cannot eat after giving blood.`,answer:!1},{text:`A campaign attracted many new donors.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-185`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "There is no swimming pool", "beach umbrellas for free", "fully booked in August".`,passage:`The Hotel Miramar is on a quiet beach in the south of Spain. Its rooms are simple but clean, and each one has a small balcony with a view of the sea. Breakfast is served on the terrace from eight to ten. There is no swimming pool, but guests can use the beach umbrellas for free. Most visitors are families who return every year, and the hotel is usually fully booked in August.`,statements:[{text:`The hotel has a swimming pool.`,answer:!1},{text:`Guests can use beach umbrellas for free.`,answer:!0},{text:`The hotel is often fully booked in August.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-186`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "left his passport at home", "She rushed to the airport", "a checklist".`,passage:`When Mark arrived at the airport, he realised that he had left his passport at home. He phoned his sister, who lives nearby, and she found it on the kitchen table. She rushed to the airport, and he got it with only twenty minutes before the check-in closed. Mark says that he now has a checklist which he reads before he leaves home, and the passport is at the top.`,statements:[{text:`Mark lost his passport in the airport.`,answer:!1},{text:`His sister brought the passport.`,answer:!0},{text:`Mark now uses a checklist.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-187`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "live longer", "as harmful to health as smoking", "prescribe activities".`,passage:`A study found that people who have regular contact with friends and family live longer on average. Loneliness, on the other hand, can be as harmful to health as smoking. Doctors in some towns now prescribe activities such as gardening or choir singing for patients who feel isolated. The patients meet new people, and many of them report that they feel happier and need fewer medicines.`,statements:[{text:`Social contact can help people live longer.`,answer:!0},{text:`Loneliness is harmless.`,answer:!1},{text:`Doctors in some towns recommend group activities.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-188`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "pay extra for suitcases", "close together", "reading the conditions carefully".`,passage:`Budget airlines have made flying cheaper but they have also changed the experience. Passengers pay extra for suitcases, food and even choosing a seat. The planes are full, and the seats are close together. Despite this, millions of people use these airlines because the tickets are so cheap. Consumer groups advise reading the conditions carefully before booking to avoid hidden costs.`,statements:[{text:`Budget airlines charge extra for some services.`,answer:!0},{text:`The seats are very spacious.`,answer:!1},{text:`Consumer groups say to read the conditions.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-189`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "arrives two hours early", "finished many books", "goes for a walk through the terminal".`,passage:`Few people enjoy waiting at the airport, but my friend Lucy has found a way to make the time useful. She arrives two hours early, finds a quiet corner and reads. She says she has finished many books in airports. If she has a long wait between flights, she often goes for a walk through the terminal or writes postcards. Lucy believes that if you accept the delay and use the time well, travelling is much less stressful.`,statements:[{text:`Lucy hates airports.`,answer:!1},{text:`She arrives early on purpose.`,answer:!0},{text:`She uses waiting time for reading and walking.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-190`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "heat its public swimming pool with the energy", "saves thousands of euros", "Engineers from other countries have visited".`,passage:`A town in Sweden has decided to heat its public swimming pool with the energy produced by a nearby data centre. The computers create a lot of heat which was previously wasted. Now it is sent through pipes to warm the water. The town saves thousands of euros a year, and the pool produces fewer emissions. Engineers from other countries have visited to see how the system works.`,statements:[{text:`The swimming pool uses heat from computers.`,answer:!0},{text:`The system increases the cost of the pool.`,answer:!1},{text:`Other countries are interested in the system.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-191`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "all year round", "rely on artificial snow", "may have to close".`,passage:`The Alps are popular all year round. In winter, skiers fill the resorts, while in summer, walkers and cyclists arrive to enjoy the cool mountain air. Many villages have built new cable cars so that visitors can reach the peaks easily. However, melting snow is a serious problem, and some ski stations now rely on artificial snow. Experts warn that, without action on climate change, many low-altitude resorts may have to close.`,statements:[{text:`The Alps attract visitors only in winter.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some ski stations use artificial snow.`,answer:!0},{text:`Experts say the future of low resorts is secure.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-192`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "before the term starts", "tour the building", "less nervous".`,passage:`The first day at a new school can be frightening. Pupils worry about making friends, finding classrooms and keeping up with the work. Many schools now organise an orientation day before the term starts. New pupils meet their teachers, tour the building and take part in games to get to know each other. Parents report that their children are less nervous on the first morning.`,statements:[{text:`Orientation days take place after the term starts.`,answer:!1},{text:`Pupils tour the building.`,answer:!0},{text:`Children are less worried afterwards.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-193`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "dangerous or repetitive tasks", "trained to supervise the machines", "become cheaper and more widespread".`,passage:`Robots are increasingly used in factories to carry out dangerous or repetitive tasks. They can lift heavy objects, weld metal and paint cars with great precision. Workers, who used to do these jobs, are now trained to supervise the machines or to repair them. Trade unions have asked companies to guarantee jobs and to offer retraining. Experts predict that robots will become cheaper and more widespread.`,statements:[{text:`Robots are used for dangerous tasks.`,answer:!0},{text:`Workers have been replaced and receive no training.`,answer:!1},{text:`Robots will probably become cheaper.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-194`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "for the first time in twenty years", "more than three per cent", "Parents are divided".`,passage:`Teachers all over the country have gone on strike for the first time in twenty years. They are demanding higher salaries and smaller classes. The government says it cannot afford to raise salaries by more than three per cent. Parents are divided: some support the teachers, while others are angry that their children are missing lessons. Union leaders say that the strike will continue until a fair agreement is reached.`,statements:[{text:`The strike is the first in twenty years.`,answer:!0},{text:`The government offered a big raise.`,answer:!1},{text:`Parents have different opinions.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-195`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "famous for its environmental policies", "closed to cars", "send delegations to Freiburg".`,passage:`The town of Freiburg in Germany is famous for its environmental policies. Many houses have solar panels on the roof, and a large part of the energy comes from the sun and the wind. The city centre is closed to cars, and trams run every few minutes. Visitors are often surprised to see how many people cycle, even in winter. Other cities send delegations to Freiburg to learn how it has created such a clean and quiet environment.`,statements:[{text:`Freiburg is known for its environmental policies.`,answer:!0},{text:`Cars are allowed everywhere in the centre.`,answer:!1},{text:`Other cities visit Freiburg to learn from it.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-196`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "every evening", "played in public for the first time", "not talent but regular practice".`,passage:`Daniel has been learning to play the guitar for two years. He practises for half an hour every evening, even when he is tired. At first his fingers hurt and the sounds he produced were terrible, but he did not give up. Last month he played in public for the first time at a small café, and the audience clapped loudly. Daniel says that the most important thing is not talent but regular practice.`,statements:[{text:`Daniel practises only on weekends.`,answer:!1},{text:`He played in public last month.`,answer:!0},{text:`Daniel believes regular practice matters more than talent.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-197`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "collects old maps", "the town as a tiny village", "lends them to the local museum".`,passage:`My neighbour has an unusual hobby: he collects old maps. He keeps them in large drawers and, on weekends, takes them out to study the places that no longer exist. He has maps from the 1700s that show the town as a tiny village. Sometimes he lends them to the local museum for exhibitions. He says that each map tells a story and that he could look at them for hours.`,statements:[{text:`The neighbour collects stamps.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some maps show a smaller version of the town.`,answer:!0},{text:`He sometimes lends maps to a museum.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-198`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "long queues every morning", "takes two days to prepare", "closes at one o'clock".`,passage:`The new bakery in our town has long queues every morning, and it is easy to see why. The owner uses an old recipe for sourdough bread which takes two days to prepare. He also makes small cakes decorated with fruit. The prices are slightly higher than in the supermarket, but customers say that the quality is worth it. The bakery closes at one o'clock because by then everything is sold out.`,statements:[{text:`The bakery is quiet in the morning.`,answer:!1},{text:`The bread takes two days to prepare.`,answer:!0},{text:`The bakery stays open all afternoon.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-199`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Because my phone was broken", "The first two days were difficult", "I now use it much less".`,passage:`Because my phone was broken, I decided to spend a week without any screens. The first two days were difficult: I kept reaching for the phone to check the time or look at messages. By the third day I felt calmer, and I started reading in the evenings. I also called my friends instead of texting them, and we had longer, more interesting conversations. At the end of the week I bought a new phone, but I now use it much less.`,statements:[{text:`The writer decided to avoid screens before the phone broke.`,answer:!1},{text:`The first days were hard.`,answer:!0},{text:`The writer uses the new phone less than before.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-200`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Opened in 1863", "a card that gives cheaper fares", "all night at weekends".`,passage:`London's underground, known as "the Tube", is the oldest metro system in the world. Opened in 1863, it now carries millions of passengers every day. Locals say that the best way to avoid crowds is to travel outside the rush hour. Visitors can buy a card that gives cheaper fares than single tickets. Some lines run all night at weekends.`,statements:[{text:`The Tube opened in the twentieth century.`,answer:!1},{text:`A card gives cheaper fares.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some lines run at night on weekends.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-201`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "from all over the world", "roads are closed for the whole morning", "just over two hours".`,passage:`The marathon in our city takes place every April. Runners from all over the world take part, and thousands of spectators line the streets to cheer. Hotels are full, and restaurants prepare special menus with pasta. Some residents complain that the roads are closed for the whole morning, but most enjoy the atmosphere. Last year, the winner finished the race in just over two hours.`,statements:[{text:`Only local people run in the marathon.`,answer:!1},{text:`Many roads are closed on race day.`,answer:!0},{text:`The winner took over four hours.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-202`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "a zone for small children", "parking is free", "worry about traffic and noise".`,passage:`A new theme park has opened near our town, and thousands of families have visited it. It has roller coasters, water slides and a zone for small children. The entrance ticket is expensive, but parking is free. Tourists enjoy the park, but some locals worry about traffic and noise. The council has promised to build a new road to reduce congestion.`,statements:[{text:`The park is only for adults.`,answer:!1},{text:`Parking costs extra.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some local people are worried about traffic.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-203`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "When she was fifteen", "warm clothes for homeless people", "more than fifty volunteers".`,passage:`When she was fifteen, Sophie started a small charity to collect warm clothes for homeless people. She asked her classmates to bring jackets and gloves they no longer needed. In the first winter, the group gave away two hundred items. Today the charity has more than fifty volunteers and works with three shelters. Sophie, now twenty-two, says that the best thing about the project is meeting people who are grateful for even the smallest help.`,statements:[{text:`Sophie began the charity as a child of twelve.`,answer:!1},{text:`The charity collects clothes for homeless people.`,answer:!0},{text:`Sophie works alone.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-204`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "worked in the nineteenth century", "forgotten for a hundred years", "A computer language ... bear her name".`,passage:`The first computer programmer in history was a woman, Ada Lovelace, who worked in the nineteenth century. She wrote instructions for a machine that had not yet been built. Her ideas were forgotten for a hundred years, but today she is considered a pioneer. A computer language and many awards bear her name.`,statements:[{text:`Ada Lovelace lived in the nineteenth century.`,answer:!0},{text:`Her ideas were immediately famous.`,answer:!1},{text:`A computer language is named after her.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-205`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Instead of rows of desks", "complain about noise", "experimenting with solutions".`,passage:`Many offices have been redesigned in recent years. Instead of rows of desks, employees now find sofas, quiet corners and standing tables. The aim is to make people more creative and to encourage them to talk to each other. Some workers like the change, but others complain about noise and the lack of privacy. Companies are experimenting with solutions, such as booths where staff can make private calls.`,statements:[{text:`The new offices have traditional rows of desks.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some employees complain about noise.`,answer:!0},{text:`Companies are trying to solve the problems.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-206`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "for fifty years", "a street party every summer", "food from many countries".`,passage:`Mrs Alvarez has lived in the same house for fifty years. She remembers when the street was only a dusty road and when the neighbours would sit outside in the evenings to talk. Today, she says, people hurry past without saying hello. To change this, she has started to organise a street party every summer. This year, more than a hundred people came, bringing food from many countries. Several new friendships began that day.`,statements:[{text:`Mrs Alvarez moved to the house recently.`,answer:!1},{text:`She organises a summer street party.`,answer:!0},{text:`People brought food from different countries.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-207`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "replaced its paper manuals with tablets", "Some older employees were unsure", "factories abroad".`,passage:`A company in Germany has replaced its paper manuals with tablets. Workers on the production line scan a code on each machine and get video instructions instantly. The change has reduced errors and has saved thousands of sheets of paper. Some older employees were unsure at first, but they received training and now say that the system is easier than reading long instructions. The management plans to introduce the same system in its factories abroad.`,statements:[{text:`The company now uses tablets instead of paper manuals.`,answer:!0},{text:`All employees welcomed the change immediately.`,answer:!1},{text:`The company wants to use the system in other countries.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-208`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "repeat parts they didn't understand", "only about one in five", "fixed study schedule".`,passage:`Online learning has become very popular. Students can follow lectures at any time and repeat parts they didn't understand. However, many find it hard to stay motivated without a teacher in front of them. A study of 5,000 learners found that only about one in five completes an online course. Those who succeed usually have a fixed study schedule and contact other students through discussion forums.`,statements:[{text:`Online students cannot repeat parts of a lecture.`,answer:!1},{text:`Most online learners complete their courses.`,answer:!1},{text:`Successful learners often have a regular schedule.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-209`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "depend on donations", "donate their time or skills", "extremely valuable".`,passage:`Charities often depend on donations from individuals. Instead of giving money, some people now donate their time or skills. A lawyer may offer free advice to people who cannot afford it, and a graphic designer can create posters for a local charity. Organisations say that such skilled volunteers are extremely valuable and that they often become lifelong supporters.`,statements:[{text:`Charities rely on donations.`,answer:!0},{text:`Only money is useful to charities.`,answer:!1},{text:`Skilled volunteers help charities.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-210`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "in his spare time", "has grown to several thousand", "asked him to produce a series".`,passage:`Rob started a podcast about local history in his spare time. He interviews older residents, who tell stories about the town long ago. The first episodes had only a handful of listeners, but the audience has grown to several thousand. A local museum has asked him to produce a series for its website. Rob still works as an accountant, but he hopes that one day he'll be able to do the podcast full time.`,statements:[{text:`Rob does the podcast as his main job.`,answer:!1},{text:`The number of listeners has increased.`,answer:!0},{text:`A museum has asked for a series.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-211`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "ended in a burnt pan", "watched videos online", "plans to attend an evening class".`,passage:`Learning to cook was a challenge for Peter when he moved out of his parents' house. His first attempt at making pasta ended in a burnt pan and a smoke alarm. Since then he has watched videos online and now prepares simple dishes such as omelettes and soups. He still can't make desserts, but his friends have stopped complaining about his cooking. He plans to attend an evening class in the autumn.`,statements:[{text:`Peter was a good cook from the beginning.`,answer:!1},{text:`He learned from videos.`,answer:!0},{text:`He is planning to take a class.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-212`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "an online bank", "answering questions from customers", "finishes the day exhausted".`,passage:`Sarah works as a customer service adviser for an online bank. She starts at eight and spends the day answering questions from customers by phone and email. Some people are polite, but others are angry because they have lost their cards or cannot access their accounts. Sarah says that the secret is to stay calm and to listen carefully. She enjoys the feeling of solving a problem, although she sometimes finishes the day exhausted. After work she goes to the gym to clear her head.`,statements:[{text:`Sarah works in a school.`,answer:!1},{text:`She helps customers with problems.`,answer:!0},{text:`She never feels tired after work.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-213`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "protect nature", "small lodges", "long flights produce a lot of pollution".`,passage:`Ecotourism is a form of travel that aims to protect nature and help local people. Visitors stay in small lodges built with local materials and are guided by residents who know the area well. Part of the price goes to conservation projects. Critics, however, say that even a small number of tourists can disturb wildlife and that long flights produce a lot of pollution.`,statements:[{text:`Ecotourism wants to protect nature.`,answer:!0},{text:`Visitors stay in large luxury hotels.`,answer:!1},{text:`Critics think flights cause pollution.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-214`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "retired people", "rent a small plot", "meeting point for neighbours".`,passage:`The community garden in our neighbourhood was started by a group of retired people. They transformed an empty piece of land into a place where residents grow vegetables and flowers. Families without gardens can rent a small plot for a few euros a year. Every autumn the gardeners organise a harvest festival with music and food. The garden has become a meeting point for neighbours who had never spoken before.`,statements:[{text:`The garden was created by young students.`,answer:!1},{text:`Families can rent a plot.`,answer:!0},{text:`Neighbours meet at the garden.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-215`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "never uses a recipe book", "watching her own mother", "start to write down her recipes".`,passage:`My grandmother never uses a recipe book. She learned to cook when she was a young girl by watching her own mother, and she remembers every dish by heart. On Sundays the whole family goes to her house, and she prepares a huge lunch with at least four courses. She says that the secret is to use fresh ingredients and to cook slowly. My cousins and I have started to write down her recipes before she forgets to teach us the little tricks she uses.`,statements:[{text:`The grandmother uses a recipe book.`,answer:!1},{text:`She learned to cook from her mother.`,answer:!0},{text:`The grandchildren are recording her recipes.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-216`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "largest coral reef", "rising sea temperatures", "avoid touching the reef".`,passage:`The Great Barrier Reef in Australia is the largest coral reef in the world. It is home to thousands of species of fish, turtles and sharks. Sadly, rising sea temperatures have caused large areas of coral to turn white and die. Scientists are working on methods to help the coral recover, and the government has limited fishing in some zones. Tour companies take visitors diving but teach them how to avoid touching the reef.`,statements:[{text:`The Great Barrier Reef is small.`,answer:!1},{text:`Rising temperatures damage the coral.`,answer:!0},{text:`Tourists are taught not to touch the reef.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-217`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "once a week", "elderly people who live alone", "hopes to extend it to the whole region".`,passage:`The local hospital has started a programme to help elderly people who live alone. Nurses visit them once a week to check their health and talk about any problems. Volunteers also call them every day to make sure they are well. One woman, aged ninety-one, says that the calls are the best part of her day. The programme costs very little, and the hospital hopes to extend it to the whole region next year.`,statements:[{text:`Nurses visit the elderly people every day.`,answer:!1},{text:`The programme helps people who live by themselves.`,answer:!0},{text:`The hospital plans to extend the programme.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-218`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "charges in five minutes", "still expensive", "how the batteries will be recycled".`,passage:`A team of scientists has developed a battery that charges in five minutes. The battery could be used in mobile phones and electric cars. Tests have been successful, but the technology is still expensive to produce. The company expects to sell the first products in about three years. Environmentalists welcome the news but ask how the batteries will be recycled.`,statements:[{text:`The new battery charges slowly.`,answer:!1},{text:`The technology is cheap.`,answer:!1},{text:`Environmentalists have a question about recycling.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-219`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "second-hand clothes", "selling some of his creations", "bought him a sewing machine".`,passage:`My teenage brother is obsessed with fashion. He spends hours choosing his outfits and often buys second-hand clothes online, then changes them with a needle and thread. His friends ask him for advice, and he has started selling some of his creations on a website. Our parents were sceptical at first, but they are now proud of him and have bought him a sewing machine.`,statements:[{text:`The brother buys only new clothes.`,answer:!1},{text:`He sells some of his designs.`,answer:!0},{text:`Their parents have supported him.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-220`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "thought that I was bad at drawing", "carry a notebook with me everywhere", "In ten weeks".`,passage:`I always thought that I was bad at drawing, but a friend persuaded me to try a beginners' class. The teacher said that anyone can learn if they look carefully, and she was right. In ten weeks I learned to draw faces, hands and simple landscapes. I am not a great artist, but my drawings have improved, and I now carry a notebook with me everywhere. It has changed the way I look at the world.`,statements:[{text:`The writer was confident about drawing at first.`,answer:!1},{text:`The writer now takes a notebook everywhere.`,answer:!0},{text:`The course lasted ten weeks.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-221`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "everybody has a different schedule", "on Saturday evening", "made the family closer".`,passage:`Many families struggle to find time to eat together. In the Johnson family, everybody has a different schedule: the parents work shifts and the children have after-school activities. They decided to introduce one rule: on Saturday evening, everyone must be at home for dinner. The family cook together, and nobody is allowed to use a phone. Mrs Johnson says that this simple habit has made the family closer.`,statements:[{text:`The Johnsons have identical timetables.`,answer:!1},{text:`They have a weekly family dinner.`,answer:!0},{text:`Mrs Johnson thinks the habit has had no effect.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-222`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "without problems", "spent the rest of the night in the car", "want to go camping again".`,passage:`Last weekend we went camping for the first time. We put up the tent without problems, but at night a storm started and water came through the roof. We spent the rest of the night in the car, laughing and eating biscuits. In the morning, the sun came out, and the children ran to the lake. Despite the bad night, everyone says they want to go camping again this summer.`,statements:[{text:`The tent was easy to put up.`,answer:!0},{text:`The family slept in the tent all night.`,answer:!1},{text:`They want to go camping again.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-223`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "in a few hours", "reduce their carbon footprint", "costs more time".`,passage:`In the past, people travelled by ship to cross the ocean, and the journey took weeks. Today, planes can do it in a few hours. However, some people are returning to slow travel. They take trains and buses instead of flying because they enjoy watching the landscape and meeting people along the way. Others do it to reduce their carbon footprint. Slow travel usually costs more time but can be cheaper.`,statements:[{text:`Today, crossing the ocean by plane takes weeks.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some people choose slow travel for the environment.`,answer:!0},{text:`Slow travel usually takes less time.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-224`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "staying in the homes of local people", "more expensive for people who live there", "introduced limits".`,passage:`There is a new trend among travellers: staying in the homes of local people instead of hotels. Websites connect visitors with hosts who rent a room or a flat. Travellers enjoy the personal contact and often pay less. But in popular cities, residents complain that the rise of this kind of rental has made flats more expensive for people who live there. Several cities have therefore introduced limits.`,statements:[{text:`Travellers rent rooms in local homes.`,answer:!0},{text:`The trend has made flats cheaper for residents.`,answer:!1},{text:`Some cities have introduced restrictions.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-225`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "dropped out", "recommended him to friends", "employs six people".`,passage:`Alex dropped out of university after one year, to the disappointment of his parents. He started a small business repairing computers from his bedroom. At first he had only a few customers, but they recommended him to friends. Today he employs six people and has a shop in the town centre. Alex says that he doesn't regret his decision, although he admits that he sometimes thinks about finishing his studies.`,statements:[{text:`Alex finished his degree.`,answer:!1},{text:`His business grew through recommendations.`,answer:!0},{text:`He has no employees.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-226`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "eat more vegetables", "the quality of the conversation matters more", "one shared meal a day".`,passage:`Eating together as a family has many benefits. Children who regularly have meals with their parents tend to eat more vegetables, do better at school and talk more about their problems. Researchers suggest that the quality of the conversation matters more than the food itself. Even in busy families, one shared meal a day can make a difference.`,statements:[{text:`Children who eat with their parents eat more vegetables.`,answer:!0},{text:`The food is more important than the conversation.`,answer:!1},{text:`One shared meal a day can help.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-227`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "it can also cause problems", "end up feeling unhappy", "recognise fake news".`,passage:`Social media can be a good way to keep in touch with friends, but it can also cause problems. Some users compare their lives with the perfect pictures that others post and end up feeling unhappy. Psychologists suggest limiting the time spent online and following accounts that make you feel positive. A school in Glasgow has started lessons where pupils learn to recognise fake news and to think carefully before they share something.`,statements:[{text:`Social media only has advantages.`,answer:!1},{text:`Comparing yourself to others online can make you unhappy.`,answer:!0},{text:`The Glasgow school teaches pupils to check information.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-228`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "nobody can leave the room", "solved faster", "go to the garden when he was angry".`,passage:`When our family has an argument, we have a simple rule: nobody can leave the room before we have all said what we feel. At first it was uncomfortable, but now we find that problems are solved faster. My father, who used to go to the garden when he was angry, says that talking is better than staying silent. Even the youngest child, who is six, can explain how she feels.`,statements:[{text:`In arguments, people can leave immediately.`,answer:!1},{text:`The rule helps to solve problems faster.`,answer:!0},{text:`The father used to leave when angry.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-229`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "human error", "train their staff", "send fake emails to test".`,passage:`Cybersecurity is a growing problem for companies. Hackers can steal customer data or demand money to release locked files. Experts say that most attacks succeed because of human error, for example when an employee opens a suspicious email. Companies therefore train their staff to recognise false messages and require passwords to be changed regularly. Some organisations even send fake emails to test their employees.`,statements:[{text:`Most successful attacks are caused by technical failures.`,answer:!1},{text:`Companies train staff to recognise suspicious messages.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some organisations send fake emails as tests.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-230`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "internal clock", "avoiding alcohol", "recover after a few days".`,passage:`Jet lag is the tiredness that many people feel after flying across several time zones. It happens because the body's internal clock is still set to the time at home. Doctors suggest drinking plenty of water, avoiding alcohol during the flight and going out into the daylight on arrival. Some travellers try to adjust their sleep a few days before the trip. Most people recover after a few days.`,statements:[{text:`Jet lag is caused by the body's internal clock.`,answer:!0},{text:`Doctors recommend drinking alcohol on the plane.`,answer:!1},{text:`Most people recover in a few days.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-231`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "being raised", "live longer", "reduce their hours gradually".`,passage:`In some countries the retirement age is being raised because people live longer. A man who retires at sixty-five may live for another twenty years. Governments say that they cannot afford to pay pensions for so long. Many workers, however, are unhappy about working until they are older, especially those in physically demanding jobs. Unions are asking for flexible solutions so that people can reduce their hours gradually.`,statements:[{text:`The retirement age is being lowered.`,answer:!1},{text:`People live longer than before.`,answer:!0},{text:`Unions suggest gradual reduction of hours.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-232`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "difficult to make friends", "made a Spanish omelette", "has attended every month".`,passage:`When Maria moved to a new country, she found it difficult to make friends. She did not speak the language well, and people seemed cold. A neighbour invited her to a community cooking evening, where everybody brought a dish from their country. Maria made a Spanish omelette and was surprised by how many people wanted the recipe. Since then she has attended every month, and she now has a group of friends who meet weekly for a walk.`,statements:[{text:`Maria found it easy to make friends at first.`,answer:!1},{text:`She cooked a Spanish dish at the community evening.`,answer:!0},{text:`She stopped going to the evenings.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-233`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "northern Spain", "simple hostels", "many people walk only a section".`,passage:`Every year, thousands of people walk the Camino de Santiago, a pilgrimage route across northern Spain. Some do it for religious reasons, others for adventure or to spend time with themselves. The walkers sleep in simple hostels, where they share meals and stories with strangers. The whole route takes about a month, but many people walk only a section. Almost all say that the experience changes the way they see their lives.`,statements:[{text:`The Camino is a route in southern Spain.`,answer:!1},{text:`Walkers sleep in hostels.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some walkers do only part of the route.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-234`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "for twenty years", "the most difficult part", "look after their own health too".`,passage:`Helen has been working as a nurse for twenty years. She works night shifts three times a week and looks after patients with serious illnesses. She says that the most difficult part of the job is telling relatives bad news. However, she also feels proud when a patient recovers and goes home. She advises young people who want to become nurses to be patient, to listen carefully and to look after their own health too.`,statements:[{text:`Helen has worked as a nurse for a long time.`,answer:!0},{text:`She finds telling bad news easy.`,answer:!1},{text:`She advises nurses to take care of themselves.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-235`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "receive a discount", "bakes cakes every morning", "on Friday evenings there is live music".`,passage:`A new coffee shop has opened on our street, and it is already popular. Customers can bring their own cups and receive a discount. The owner bakes cakes every morning, and the smell of fresh bread fills the whole street. In the afternoons, students sit at the large wooden tables with their laptops, and on Friday evenings there is live music. The owner says he wanted to create a place where people feel at home.`,statements:[{text:`Customers get a discount if they bring their own cup.`,answer:!0},{text:`The cakes are bought from a factory.`,answer:!1},{text:`Live music is played on Fridays.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-236`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Claire disagrees", "freezes any leftovers", "the most relaxing part of her day".`,passage:`A lot of people think that cooking for one person is not worth the effort. Claire disagrees. She lives alone and enjoys making a proper dinner every night. She plans her meals on Sundays, buys fresh vegetables twice a week and freezes any leftovers for busy days. Claire says that the time she spends in the kitchen is the most relaxing part of her day, and that eating well on her own is a way of looking after herself.`,statements:[{text:`Claire thinks cooking for one is a waste of time.`,answer:!1},{text:`She freezes leftovers.`,answer:!0},{text:`She finds cooking relaxing.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-237`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "works from home", "has no paid holidays", "the freedom makes up for the insecurity".`,passage:`Daniela is a freelance translator. She works from home, sets her own hours and chooses her projects. However, she must find her own clients and has no paid holidays. In busy months, she works until midnight, while in quiet months she worries about money. Daniela says that the freedom makes up for the insecurity, and she can't imagine working in an office again.`,statements:[{text:`Daniela works in an office.`,answer:!1},{text:`She receives paid holidays.`,answer:!1},{text:`She values freedom.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-238`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "becoming scarce", "collect water from a tank", "a bucket instead of a hose".`,passage:`In many parts of the world, water is becoming scarce. Rivers are drying up because of climate change, and farmers are finding it harder to grow crops. In one Spanish village, residents must now collect water from a tank that is filled once a week by lorry. Scientists suggest that people can help by taking shorter showers, repairing leaking taps and using a bucket instead of a hose to wash the car.`,statements:[{text:`Water is becoming easier to find.`,answer:!1},{text:`The Spanish villagers get water from a tank.`,answer:!0},{text:`Scientists suggest using a hose to wash cars.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-239`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "Larger supermarkets do not accept", "support small businesses", "more than a hundred shops".`,passage:`The town of Totnes in England has started its own local currency, called the "Totnes pound". Residents can exchange pounds for Totnes pounds and spend them in local shops. The aim is to keep money in the community and support small businesses. Larger supermarkets do not accept the currency. After five years, more than a hundred shops take part, and the organisers say that the town centre is livelier than before.`,statements:[{text:`The Totnes pound is accepted by large supermarkets.`,answer:!1},{text:`The aim is to support small local businesses.`,answer:!0},{text:`More than a hundred shops take part.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-240`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "looked more like a hat", "relaxing", "gives to friends as gifts".`,passage:`Anna was looking for a hobby when a friend suggested trying pottery. She joined a weekly class and, although her first bowl looked more like a hat, she found the work relaxing. Over the months her skills have improved. She now makes plates and mugs that she gives to friends as gifts. Anna says that touching the clay helps her to forget the stress of the office.`,statements:[{text:`Anna's first bowl was perfect.`,answer:!1},{text:`Pottery helps her to relax.`,answer:!0},{text:`She gives away what she makes.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-241`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "one person goes to the supermarket", "divide the cost equally", "At first they argued".`,passage:`Julia and her flatmates have a system for shopping. Every Sunday they write a list of what they need, and one person goes to the supermarket while the others clean the flat. They keep all the receipts in a box and, at the end of the month, they divide the cost equally. At first they argued about who should buy the expensive items, such as cleaning products, but they solved the problem by buying those together once every three months. Julia says the system is simple and saves a lot of time.`,statements:[{text:`The flatmates go shopping together every Sunday.`,answer:!1},{text:`They share the cost of shopping equally.`,answer:!0},{text:`They never argued about money.`,answer:!1}]},{id:`b1-tf-242`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "interactive exhibitions", "attendance has risen", "could distract people".`,passage:`Museums are changing. Instead of simply displaying objects behind glass, many now offer interactive exhibitions in which visitors can touch, listen and play. Children particularly enjoy these new spaces, and attendance has risen. Some curators worry that technology could distract people from the real objects. They argue that screens should be used carefully and that the original works must remain the centre of the visit.`,statements:[{text:`Museums only display objects behind glass.`,answer:!1},{text:`Attendance has increased.`,answer:!0},{text:`Some curators are concerned about technology.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-243`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "flat", "a different village", "strong enough to push them backwards".`,passage:`A group of friends decided to spend their holiday cycling across the Netherlands. They carried only small bags, and each night they stayed in a different village. The land is flat and the cycle paths are excellent, so they covered about eighty kilometres a day with little effort. The only problem was the wind, which was sometimes strong enough to push them backwards. At the end of the week they were tired but proud.`,statements:[{text:`The land was hilly.`,answer:!1},{text:`They stayed in a different village each night.`,answer:!0},{text:`Wind caused difficulties.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-244`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`work-education-technology`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "two hundred jobs", "cost of housing has risen", "build more affordable homes".`,passage:`An international company has moved part of its call centre to a smaller town. The change created two hundred jobs, which the town badly needed. Local shops and restaurants have benefited from the extra customers at lunchtime. However, the cost of housing has risen, and some residents say they can no longer afford to rent a flat. The mayor is looking for ways to build more affordable homes.`,statements:[{text:`The new call centre created jobs.`,answer:!0},{text:`Housing has become cheaper.`,answer:!1},{text:`The mayor wants more affordable homes.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-245`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "shows respect", "can make mistakes", "appreciate the effort".`,passage:`When you travel abroad, it is a good idea to learn a few words of the local language. Even a simple "hello" or "thank you" shows respect and often makes people friendlier. Some travellers use apps to translate, but these can make mistakes, especially in noisy places. A small phrasebook can also be useful if your phone battery runs out. Locals usually appreciate the effort, even if the pronunciation is far from perfect.`,statements:[{text:`Learning local words is not useful.`,answer:!1},{text:`Apps can make mistakes.`,answer:!0},{text:`Locals usually value the effort.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-246`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "carbon neutral", "hundreds of kilometres of bicycle lanes", "on track to achieve it".`,passage:`The city of Copenhagen aims to become carbon neutral in the next few years. It has built hundreds of kilometres of bicycle lanes and offers cheap electric buses. Many buildings are heated with energy from waste. Citizens receive information about how to reduce their own emissions, and schools teach children to sort rubbish at home. Experts say that although the goal is ambitious, the city is on track to achieve it.`,statements:[{text:`Copenhagen wants to reduce carbon emissions.`,answer:!0},{text:`The city has no bicycle lanes.`,answer:!1},{text:`Experts believe the goal can be reached.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-247`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "is rising", "melting faster", "demonstrations to demand faster action".`,passage:`Climate scientists warn that the average temperature of the Earth is rising. One result is that glaciers are melting faster, and sea levels are rising. Some islands in the Pacific may disappear in the next fifty years. Governments have agreed to reduce their emissions, but critics say that the promises are not strong enough. Meanwhile, many young people are organising demonstrations to demand faster action.`,statements:[{text:`The temperature of the Earth is going down.`,answer:!1},{text:`Glaciers are melting faster.`,answer:!0},{text:`Young people are protesting for faster action.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-248`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`travel-places-leisure`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "eighteen days", "cargo ship", "planning a similar trip".`,passage:`Last summer, Marta and Luis took a trip on a cargo ship from Spain to Brazil. They had a small cabin, ate with the crew and spent the days reading and watching the ocean. The journey took eighteen days, and they saw dolphins, flying fish and a spectacular storm. They agreed it was slower and less comfortable than a plane, but far more memorable. They are already planning a similar trip across the Pacific.`,statements:[{text:`The trip lasted about two and a half weeks.`,answer:!0},{text:`They travelled by plane.`,answer:!1},{text:`They want to make another sea voyage.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-249`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`society-health-environment`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "pollinate many of the plants we eat", "is falling", "sold in local shops".`,passage:`Bees are essential for our food supply because they pollinate many of the plants we eat. However, the number of bees is falling in many countries, partly because of pesticides. Some cities have responded by planting wildflowers in parks and on roofs. A group of beekeepers in London now keeps hives on top of office buildings. The honey they collect is sold in local shops, and the profits are used to protect wild bees.`,statements:[{text:`Bees help plants to produce fruit.`,answer:!0},{text:`The number of bees is increasing.`,answer:!1},{text:`Honey from city hives is sold locally.`,answer:!0}]},{id:`b1-tf-250`,type:`true-false`,level:`B1`,topic:`reading`,topics:[`everyday-life`],prompt:`Read the text and decide if each sentence is true or false.`,explanation:`The text says: "only twenty minutes a day", "short, regular conversations", "more confident".`,passage:`A study of busy parents showed that they spend, on average, only twenty minutes a day talking directly to their children. Much of the time at home is taken up by chores, television and phones. Psychologists recommend short, regular conversations, for example during a walk to school or while preparing dinner together. They say that children who feel listened to are more confident and do better at school.`,statements:[{text:`Parents talk to their children for a long time every day.`,answer:!1},{text:`Psychologists recommend short regular conversations.`,answer:!0},{text:`Children who are listened to are more confident.`,answer:!0}]}]};export{e as default};